/-!
# Theorem 3.6 (spheres): Bourgain–Gamburd's Theorem 1 as a named Prop, the printed reformulation refuted on `SO(2)`, isometry spherical families universal from ergodicity

`theo:universality_sphere` — `main.tex:305` (Section 3.1.3, `main.tex:295–310`; Appendix B.3,
`main.tex:823–837`). `theo:spectral_gap_sphere` — `main.tex:830` ("Reformulation of Theorem 1 of
`bourgain2012spectral`", arXiv:1108.6264v1). Neither is marked: the first holds only in corrected
forms (C-28, C-31); the second is false as printed for `SO(2)` (C-32), and the theorem it cites
is the named `Prop` `EGF.BourgainGamburdTheorem1` (DEC-141), see SCOPE.

> An isometry spherical family is a universal EGF family, provided technical assumptions on the
> $(\Phi_i)_{i=1}^p$. (`main.tex:305`)

> Assume that $(\Phi_1,\cdots, \Phi_p) \in \mathrm{SO}(d)\cap\mathrm{Mat}_{d\times d}(\overline
> {\mathbb Q})$, that the group generated by $\Phi_1,\cdots,\Phi_p$ is dense in
> $\mathrm{SO}(d,\mathbb R)$ and that $\forall i\in \{1,\cdots,p\}, \exists j \in
> \{1,\cdots,p\}, \Phi_i^{-1}=\Phi_j$. Assume that, $\forall i, \forwardalpha^i = \frac{1}{p}$
> then the associated Markov kernel $\ForwardPolicyStar$ given by equation
> \eqref{equ:forward_policy} has a spectral gap. (`main.tex:832–833`)

> With the technical condition "The set of transforms $(\Phi_i)_{i=1}^p$ is stable by inverse, the
> group generated by $(\Phi_i)_{i=1}^p$ is dense in $\mathrm{SO}(d,\mathbb R)$ and each of the
> $\Phi_i$ has algebraic coefficients", Theorem \ref{theo:universality_sphere} then follows from
> master Theorem \ref{theo:universality_true}. (`main.tex:836`)

## What is proved

| | |
|---|---|
| `measurePreserving_rotation_sphere`, `measurePreserving_rotSphere` | every linear isometry of `ℝⁿ` preserves `σ = volume.toSphere` on `S^{n−1}` |
| `BourgainGamburdTheorem1`, `bourgainGamburd_hypotheses_witness`, `bourgainGamburd_fails_trivial` | Theorem 1, faithful, a named `Prop`; its hypotheses hold for a pair in `SU(2)` (`su2Witness`, Euler angles); its conclusion fails for trivial generators |
| `SpectralGapSphereReformulation`, `not_spectralGapSphereReformulation_two`, `not_hasBGSpectralGap_sphere_two`, `so2Witness_eigen` | **C-32**: the printed reformulation, false for `SO(2)` (eigenvalues `cos kθ → 1` on `L²₀`); no finite set of rotations of `𝕊¹` has a spectral gap (C-28 (b)) |
| `ergodic_of_hasBGSpectralGap`, `universality_sphere_of_reformulation` | the route of `main.tex:836`, from the reformulation as a hypothesis |
| `IsometrySphericalModel`, `isometrySphericalFamily`, `IsIsometrySphericalFamily`, `IsRichSphericalModel` | a family as the image of a model; C-31's richness |
| `universality_sphere_of_ergodic`, `universality_sphere_iff` | **the strongest form** (C-28, C-29, C-31); ergodicity is also necessary |
| `universality_sphere_one`, `universality_sphere_one_of_dense`, `universality_sphere_one_witness` | on `𝕊¹`, one irrational rotation suffices, and density in `SO(2)` forces one; an instance |
| `not_isUniversalFamilyEps_sphere_of_constantHeads`, `UniversalitySpherePrinted`, `not_universalitySpherePrinted_one` | **C-31**: the printed Theorem 3.6 fails whenever its condition is met, in particular on `𝕊¹` |
| `not_universality_sphere_identity` | `main.tex:307`'s "algebraic and frozen" omits density: the identity refutes it |

## Hypothesis checklist

| paper hypothesis (`main.tex:305`, `:836`) | here (`universality_sphere_of_ergodic`) |
|---|---|
| `Φᵢ ∈ SO_{d+1}(ℝ)` acting on `𝕊^d` | ✓ `Φ : Fin p → SO n`, `n = d + 1`, `x ↦ Ax` |
| stable under inverse; algebraic coefficients | ⚠ weakened: dropped |
| the generated group dense in `SO(d, ℝ)` | ⚠ weakened: every set a.e.-invariant under the `Φᵢ` is null or conull |
| frozen (`main.tex:307`) | ✓ the rich model contains the uniform kernel of the given `Φ` |
| Theorem 1 of `bourgain2012spectral` | absent; `universality_sphere_of_reformulation` assumes the printed reformulation |
| an isometry spherical family (`main.tex:303`) | ⚠ weakened: any family; `isometrySphericalFamily M` is an instance |
| (unstated) the model realizes `αⁱ ≡ 1/p` and outflows dense in the non-negative cone of `L²(σ)` | ⚠ strengthened: `IsRichSphericalModel Φ 𝓕` (C-31), needed |
| "universal EGF family" | the ε-form of record `IsUniversalFamilyEps σ 𝓕` (DEC-141) |

## SCOPE (disclosed)

Readings. The "natural Riemannian volume" (`main.tex:297`) is `σ = volume.toSphere`
(`σ(A) = n · vol((0, 1) • A)`), rotation-invariant (proved), not identified with a Riemannian
volume (Mathlib has none). `SO(n)` is `Matrix.specialOrthogonalGroup (Fin n) ℝ`, subspace
topology; `𝕊^d` is `RoundSphere (d + 1)`. "Algebraic" is `IsAlgebraic ℤ` (`main.tex:826`). The
assumptions of `main.tex:305` are those of `:836` at every parameter, "dense in `SO(d, ℝ)`" read
in the group the rotations live in (C-32's index slip). A family is the image of a model
(non-empty parameters, rotations a function of the parameter, constant when frozen,
`main.tex:307`); with all rotations free, `:836` fails at the parameter `Φ ≡ 1`, so the printed
theorem is vacuous in that reading and the refutation uses frozen rotations; continuity is not
encoded; the refuting models are continuous; a one-point model refutes as well.
`BourgainGamburdTheorem1`, a hypothesis only of `bourgainGamburd_witness_gap`: `SU(d)` is
`Matrix.specialUnitaryGroup (Fin d) ℂ`, Haar probability `haarMeasure ⊤`; entries
`IsAlgebraic ℚ`; "Zariski dense in `SL_d(ℂ)`" replaced by "dense in `SU(d)`" (their footnote 1;
not formalized); "`λ₁(z)`, the supremum of the eigenvalues of `z` on the orthogonal complement of
the constants, `< 2k`" read as `∃ c < 2k, Re⟨zf, f⟩ ≤ c‖f‖²` on `L²₀`, which implies it and is
equivalent by Peter–Weyl (not formalized); any `k` (density forces `k ≥ 2`, not formalized). In
`SpectralGapSphereReformulation n` (`SO(n)` on `S^{n−1}`, the printed index) the gap is
Bourgain–Gamburd's one-sided notion for `Pf(x) = ∫ f dπ(x)` on the real `L²₀(σ)`; the Koopman
operator of `main.tex:273` is its adjoint, same quadratic form (not formalized); the refuting pair
has eigenfunctions in `L²₀(σ)` with eigenvalues `cos kθ → 1` (`so2Witness_eigen`), against the
spectral and almost-invariant readings too. Not proved: the reformulation for `n = 3`
(T-egf-spectral-gap-so3, planned); density ⇒ ergodicity for `n ≥ 3` (T-egf-sphere-dense-ergodic,
planned; `n = 2` is `universality_sphere_one_of_dense`), so for `n ≥ 3`
`universality_sphere_of_ergodic` has no instance here; density of the six `π/4` rotations of
`main.tex:496`. Imports `EGFScaffold.TorusFamilies` (`IsGroupErgodic`).

Provenance: mathlib `fabf563a` (tag `v4.31.0`), pinned via `lakefile.toml`. Bourgain–Gamburd read
off arXiv:1108.6264v1 (fetched 2026-11-21), §0 pp. 1–2 (`z`, `λ₁(z)`, Theorem 1, footnote 1).
-/

namespace EGF

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Filter Set
open scoped ENNReal NNReal Topology Pointwise Matrix ComplexConjugate

/-! ## The round sphere and its rotations -/

/-- **The round sphere** `S^{n−1} = {x ∈ ℝⁿ | ‖x‖ = 1}` (`main.tex:297`; the paper's `𝕊^d` is
`RoundSphere (d + 1)`). -/
abbrev RoundSphere (n : ℕ) : Type := Metric.sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) 1

/-- **The volume of the sphere** `σ = volume.toSphere`: `σ(A) = n · vol((0, 1) • A)`
(`Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Constructions/HaarToSphere.lean`), the reading of `main.tex:297`'s
"natural Riemannian volume measure". -/
noncomputable def sphereVolume (n : ℕ) : Measure (RoundSphere n) :=
  (volume : Measure (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))).toSphere

instance (n : ℕ) : IsFiniteMeasure (sphereVolume n) := by
  unfold sphereVolume; infer_instance

instance (n : ℕ) : (sphereVolume n).IsOpenPosMeasure := by
  unfold sphereVolume; infer_instance

/-- A linear isometry `e` of `ℝⁿ` acts on the sphere. -/
noncomputable def sphereMap {n : ℕ} (e : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))
    (x : RoundSphere n) : RoundSphere n :=
  ⟨e x, by simp⟩

@[simp] theorem coe_sphereMap {n : ℕ} (e : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))
    (x : RoundSphere n) : (sphereMap e x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) = e x := rfl

theorem continuous_sphereMap {n : ℕ}
    (e : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) : Continuous (sphereMap e) :=
  (e.continuous.comp continuous_subtype_val).subtype_mk _

theorem sphereMap_symm_apply {n : ℕ} (e : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))
    (x : RoundSphere n) : sphereMap e.symm (sphereMap e x) = x :=
  Subtype.ext (e.symm_apply_apply x)

theorem sphereMap_apply_symm {n : ℕ} (e : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))
    (x : RoundSphere n) : sphereMap e (sphereMap e.symm x) = x :=
  Subtype.ext (e.apply_symm_apply x)

/-- The homeomorphism of the sphere induced by a linear isometry. -/
noncomputable def sphereHomeo {n : ℕ}
    (e : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) : RoundSphere n ≃ₜ RoundSphere n where
  toFun := sphereMap e
  invFun := sphereMap e.symm
  left_inv := sphereMap_symm_apply e
  right_inv := sphereMap_apply_symm e
  continuous_toFun := continuous_sphereMap e
  continuous_invFun := continuous_sphereMap e.symm

/-- **A linear isometry preserves `σ`**: it preserves `volume` (`LinearIsometryEquiv.measurePreserving`)
and commutes with the cone construction, `(0, 1) • e⁻¹(A) = e⁻¹((0, 1) • A)`. -/
theorem measurePreserving_rotation_sphere {n : ℕ}
    (e : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) :
    MeasurePreserving (sphereMap e) (sphereVolume n) (sphereVolume n) := by
  have hm := (continuous_sphereMap e).measurable
  refine ⟨hm, ?_⟩
  ext s hs
  rw [Measure.map_apply hm hs]
  unfold sphereVolume
  rw [Measure.toSphere_apply' _ (hm hs), Measure.toSphere_apply' _ hs]
  congr 1
  have hset : Ioo (0 : ℝ) 1 • (((↑) : RoundSphere n → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) '' (sphereMap e ⁻¹' s))
      = e ⁻¹' (Ioo (0 : ℝ) 1 • (((↑) : RoundSphere n → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) '' s)) := by
    ext y
    simp only [Set.mem_smul, Set.mem_image, Set.mem_preimage]
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨r, hr, _, ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
      exact ⟨r, hr, _, ⟨sphereMap e x, hx, rfl⟩, by simp [map_smul]⟩
    · rintro ⟨r, hr, _, ⟨z, hz, rfl⟩, hy⟩
      refine ⟨r, hr, _, ⟨sphereMap e.symm z, by rwa [sphereMap_apply_symm], rfl⟩, ?_⟩
      apply e.injective
      rw [coe_sphereMap, map_smul, LinearIsometryEquiv.apply_symm_apply, hy]
  rw [hset]
  exact (e.measurePreserving.measure_preimage_equiv (f := e.toHomeomorph.toMeasurableEquiv) _)

/-- **`SO(n)`**: `Matrix.specialOrthogonalGroup (Fin n) ℝ`, with the subspace topology of the
matrices. -/
abbrev SO (n : ℕ) : Type := Matrix.specialOrthogonalGroup (Fin n) ℝ

/-- The linear isometry `x ↦ Ax` of `A ∈ SO(n)` (through `Matrix.toEuclideanCLM`, a star algebra
isomorphism, which sends unitaries to unitaries). -/
noncomputable def rotLIE {n : ℕ} (A : SO n) :
    EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) :=
  Unitary.linearIsometryEquiv
    ⟨Matrix.toEuclideanCLM (n := Fin n) (𝕜 := ℝ) A.1, Unitary.map_mem _ A.2.1⟩

theorem ofLp_rotLIE {n : ℕ} (A : SO n) (x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) :
    WithLp.ofLp (rotLIE A x) = (A : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ) *ᵥ WithLp.ofLp x := rfl

/-- **The rotation** `x ↦ Ax` of `S^{n−1}`, `A ∈ SO(n)`. -/
noncomputable def rotSphere {n : ℕ} (A : SO n) : RoundSphere n → RoundSphere n :=
  sphereMap (rotLIE A)

theorem rotSphere_apply_coord {n : ℕ} (A : SO n) (x : RoundSphere n) (i : Fin n) :
    (rotSphere A x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) i =
      ∑ j, (A : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ) i j * (x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) j := by
  show (WithLp.ofLp (rotLIE A x)) i = _
  rw [ofLp_rotLIE]
  rfl

theorem rotSphere_mul {n : ℕ} (A B : SO n) (x : RoundSphere n) :
    rotSphere (A * B) x = rotSphere A (rotSphere B x) := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  apply WithLp.ofLp_injective 2
  show WithLp.ofLp (rotLIE (A * B) x) = WithLp.ofLp (rotLIE A (rotLIE B x))
  rw [ofLp_rotLIE, ofLp_rotLIE, ofLp_rotLIE, Matrix.mulVec_mulVec]
  rfl

theorem rotSphere_one {n : ℕ} (x : RoundSphere n) : rotSphere 1 x = x := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  apply WithLp.ofLp_injective 2
  have h1 : ((1 : SO n) : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ) = 1 := rfl
  have h := ofLp_rotLIE (1 : SO n) x
  rw [h1, Matrix.one_mulVec] at h
  exact h

theorem continuous_rotSphere {n : ℕ} (A : SO n) : Continuous (rotSphere A) :=
  continuous_sphereMap _

theorem measurable_rotSphere {n : ℕ} (A : SO n) : Measurable (rotSphere A) :=
  (continuous_rotSphere A).measurable

theorem measurePreserving_rotSphere {n : ℕ} (A : SO n) :
    MeasurePreserving (rotSphere A) (sphereVolume n) (sphereVolume n) :=
  measurePreserving_rotation_sphere _

/-- A rotation as a permutation of the sphere. -/
noncomputable def rotPerm {n : ℕ} (A : SO n) : Equiv.Perm (RoundSphere n) where
  toFun := rotSphere A
  invFun := rotSphere A⁻¹
  left_inv x := by rw [← rotSphere_mul, inv_mul_cancel, rotSphere_one]
  right_inv x := by rw [← rotSphere_mul, mul_inv_cancel, rotSphere_one]

theorem coe_rotPerm {n : ℕ} (A : SO n) : ⇑(rotPerm A) = rotSphere A := rfl

theorem coe_rotPerm_inv {n : ℕ} (A : SO n) : ⇑(rotPerm A)⁻¹ = rotSphere A⁻¹ := rfl

/-- **Integrals on the sphere are rotation-invariant.** -/
theorem integral_comp_rotSphere {n : ℕ} (A : SO n) {G : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup G]
    [NormedSpace ℝ G] (F : RoundSphere n → G) :
    ∫ x, F (rotSphere A x) ∂(sphereVolume n) = ∫ x, F x ∂(sphereVolume n) :=
  (measurePreserving_rotSphere A).integral_comp' (f := (sphereHomeo (rotLIE A)).toMeasurableEquiv) F

/-! ## `SU(d)`, its Haar probability, and Bourgain–Gamburd's Theorem 1 -/

/-- **`SU(d)`**: `Matrix.specialUnitaryGroup (Fin d) ℂ`, with the subspace topology of the
matrices (`Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/UnitaryGroup.lean:255`). -/
abbrev SU (d : ℕ) : Type := Matrix.specialUnitaryGroup (Fin d) ℂ

/-- `SU(d)` is a topological group: multiplication is continuous and the inverse is `A ↦ A*`. -/
instance (d : ℕ) : IsTopologicalGroup (SU d) where
  toContinuousMul := Submonoid.continuousMul _
  continuous_inv := by
    have h : (fun A : SU d => ((A⁻¹ : SU d) : Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℂ)) =
        fun A : SU d => star (A : Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℂ) := rfl
    refine continuous_induced_rng.2 ?_
    rw [Function.comp_def, h]
    exact continuous_star.comp continuous_subtype_val

/-- `SU(d)` is closed in the matrices. -/
theorem isClosed_specialUnitaryGroup (d : ℕ) :
    IsClosed (Matrix.specialUnitaryGroup (Fin d) ℂ : Set (Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℂ)) := by
  have h : (Matrix.specialUnitaryGroup (Fin d) ℂ : Set (Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℂ)) =
      {A | A * star A = 1} ∩ {A | A.det = 1} := by
    ext A
    simp only [SetLike.mem_coe, Matrix.mem_specialUnitaryGroup_iff, Matrix.mem_unitaryGroup_iff,
      Set.mem_inter_iff, Set.mem_setOf_eq]
  rw [h]
  exact (isClosed_eq (continuous_id.mul continuous_star) continuous_const).inter
    (isClosed_eq (Continuous.matrix_det continuous_id) continuous_const)

/-- `SU(d)` is compact: closed, with entries of modulus at most `1`. -/
instance (d : ℕ) : CompactSpace (SU d) := by
  refine isCompact_iff_compactSpace.mp ?_
  have hsub : (Matrix.specialUnitaryGroup (Fin d) ℂ : Set (Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℂ)) ⊆
      Set.pi univ fun _ => Set.pi univ fun _ => Metric.closedBall (0 : ℂ) 1 := by
    intro A hA i _ j _
    rw [Metric.mem_closedBall, dist_zero_right]
    exact entry_norm_bound_of_unitary (Matrix.mem_specialUnitaryGroup_iff.1 hA).1 i j
  exact (isCompact_univ_pi fun _ => isCompact_univ_pi fun _ => isCompact_closedBall _ _).of_isClosed_subset
    (isClosed_specialUnitaryGroup d) hsub

/-- The Borel σ-algebra of `SU(d)`. -/
noncomputable instance (d : ℕ) : MeasurableSpace (SU d) := borel _

instance (d : ℕ) : BorelSpace (SU d) := ⟨rfl⟩

/-- **The Haar probability of `SU(d)`** (`haarMeasure ⊤`, normalized on the whole compact group). -/
noncomputable def suHaar (d : ℕ) : Measure (SU d) := Measure.haarMeasure ⊤

instance (d : ℕ) : (suHaar d).IsHaarMeasure := Measure.isHaarMeasure_haarMeasure _

instance (d : ℕ) : IsProbabilityMeasure (suHaar d) := ⟨by
  have h := Measure.haarMeasure_self (K₀ := (⊤ : TopologicalSpace.PositiveCompacts (SU d)))
  simpa [suHaar] using h⟩

/-- **The Hecke operator** of Bourgain–Gamburd (arXiv:1108.6264v1, p. 1):
`z f(x) = ∑ⱼ (f(gⱼ x) + f(gⱼ⁻¹ x))`. -/
noncomputable def heckeOp {d k : ℕ} (g : Fin k → SU d) (f : SU d → ℂ) (x : SU d) : ℂ :=
  ∑ j, (f (g j * x) + f ((g j)⁻¹ * x))

/-- **Theorem 1 of Bourgain–Gamburd** (arXiv:1108.6264v1, p. 2; the theorem `main.tex:830` cites),
the named external result of DEC-141: for `d ≥ 2` and `g₁, …, g_k ∈ SU(d)` with algebraic entries
generating a dense subgroup of `SU(d)` (their footnote 1's equivalent of Zariski density in
`SL_d(ℂ)`), the Hecke operator has a spectral gap: some `c < 2k` bounds `Re⟨zf, f⟩ ≤ c‖f‖²` on the
orthogonal complement of the constants in `L²(SU(d))`. A `Prop`, never an axiom, a hypothesis of
nothing in this file but `bourgainGamburd_witness_gap`. -/
def BourgainGamburdTheorem1 : Prop :=
  ∀ (d : ℕ), 2 ≤ d → ∀ (k : ℕ) (g : Fin k → SU d),
    (∀ j a b, IsAlgebraic ℚ ((g j : Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℂ) a b)) →
    Dense ((Subgroup.closure (Set.range g) : Subgroup (SU d)) : Set (SU d)) →
    ∃ c : ℝ, c < 2 * k ∧ ∀ f : SU d → ℂ, MemLp f 2 (suHaar d) → ∫ x, f x ∂(suHaar d) = 0 →
      (∫ x, heckeOp g f x * conj (f x) ∂(suHaar d)).re ≤ c * ∫ x, ‖f x‖ ^ 2 ∂(suHaar d)

/-- The element `diag(−1, −1, 1, …, 1)` of `SU(d)`, `d ≥ 2`. -/
noncomputable def suFlip (d : ℕ) : Matrix (Fin (d + 2)) (Fin (d + 2)) ℂ :=
  Matrix.diagonal fun i => if (i : ℕ) ≤ 1 then -1 else 1

theorem suFlip_mem (d : ℕ) : suFlip d ∈ Matrix.specialUnitaryGroup (Fin (d + 2)) ℂ := by
  rw [Matrix.mem_specialUnitaryGroup_iff, Matrix.mem_unitaryGroup_iff]
  refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [suFlip, Matrix.star_eq_conjTranspose, Matrix.diagonal_conjTranspose, Matrix.diagonal_mul_diagonal,
      ← Matrix.diagonal_one]
    congr 1
    funext i
    by_cases h : (i : ℕ) ≤ 1 <;> simp [h]
  · rw [suFlip, Matrix.det_diagonal, Fin.prod_univ_succ, Fin.prod_univ_succ]
    simp


/-- **`L²₀(SU(d)) ≠ 0`** for `d ≥ 2`: the entry `x ↦ x₀₀` is bounded, has mean zero (left
translation by `diag(−1, −1, 1, …)` changes its sign) and positive norm (it does not vanish near
`1`, and the Haar measure charges open sets). -/
theorem exists_meanZero_SU {d : ℕ} (hd : 2 ≤ d) :
    ∃ f : SU d → ℂ, MemLp f 2 (suHaar d) ∧ ∫ x, f x ∂(suHaar d) = 0 ∧
      0 < ∫ x, ‖f x‖ ^ 2 ∂(suHaar d) := by
  obtain ⟨d', rfl⟩ : ∃ d', d = d' + 2 := ⟨d - 2, by omega⟩
  set f : SU (d' + 2) → ℂ := fun x => (x : Matrix (Fin (d' + 2)) (Fin (d' + 2)) ℂ) 0 0 with hfdef
  have hcont : Continuous f := (continuous_subtype_val).matrix_elem 0 0
  have hbound : ∀ x, ‖f x‖ ≤ 1 := fun x =>
    entry_norm_bound_of_unitary (Matrix.mem_specialUnitaryGroup_iff.1 x.2).1 0 0
  refine ⟨f, MemLp.of_bound hcont.aestronglyMeasurable 1 (ae_of_all _ hbound), ?_, ?_⟩
  · set D : SU (d' + 2) := ⟨suFlip d', suFlip_mem d'⟩
    have hD : ∀ x, f (D * x) = -f x := by
      intro x
      simp [hfdef, D, suFlip, Matrix.diagonal_mul]
    have h := integral_mul_left_eq_self (μ := suHaar (d' + 2)) f D
    simp_rw [hD, integral_neg] at h
    linear_combination (-1 / 2 : ℂ) * h
  · have hint : Integrable (fun x => ‖f x‖ ^ 2) (suHaar (d' + 2)) :=
      Integrable.of_bound (hcont.norm.pow 2).aestronglyMeasurable 1 (ae_of_all _ fun x => by
        rw [Real.norm_eq_abs, abs_of_nonneg (by positivity)]
        exact pow_le_one₀ (norm_nonneg _) (hbound x))
    rw [integral_pos_iff_support_of_nonneg (fun x => by positivity) hint]
    have hU : IsOpen {x : SU (d' + 2) | f x ≠ 0} := isOpen_ne_fun hcont continuous_const
    have h1 : (1 : SU (d' + 2)) ∈ {x : SU (d' + 2) | f x ≠ 0} := by
      simp [hfdef]
    refine (hU.measure_pos _ ⟨1, h1⟩).trans_le (measure_mono fun x hx => ?_)
    simp only [Function.mem_support]
    exact pow_ne_zero 2 (norm_ne_zero_iff.2 hx)

/-- **The conclusion of `BourgainGamburdTheorem1` is not trivial**: for `d ≥ 2` and the trivial
generators `gⱼ = 1` (which violate its density hypothesis), `z = 2k` and no `c < 2k` works. -/
theorem bourgainGamburd_fails_trivial {d : ℕ} (hd : 2 ≤ d) (k : ℕ) :
    ¬ ∃ c : ℝ, c < 2 * k ∧ ∀ f : SU d → ℂ, MemLp f 2 (suHaar d) → ∫ x, f x ∂(suHaar d) = 0 →
      (∫ x, heckeOp (fun _ : Fin k => (1 : SU d)) f x * conj (f x) ∂(suHaar d)).re ≤
        c * ∫ x, ‖f x‖ ^ 2 ∂(suHaar d) := by
  rintro ⟨c, hc, h⟩
  obtain ⟨f, hf, hf0, hpos⟩ := exists_meanZero_SU hd
  have hle := h f hf hf0
  have hz : ∀ x, heckeOp (fun _ : Fin k => (1 : SU d)) f x * conj (f x) =
      ((2 * k * ‖f x‖ ^ 2 : ℝ) : ℂ) := by
    intro x
    simp only [heckeOp, inv_one, one_mul, Finset.sum_const, Finset.card_univ, Fintype.card_fin,
      nsmul_eq_mul]
    push_cast
    rw [← Complex.mul_conj']
    ring
  simp_rw [hz] at hle
  rw [integral_complex_ofReal, Complex.ofReal_re, integral_const_mul] at hle
  nlinarith

/-! ## The uniform EGF kernel of rotations and Bourgain–Gamburd's one-sided spectral gap -/

/-- **The integral of a function against the EGF kernel** `π(x) = ∑ᵢ αⁱ(x) δ_{Φᵢ(x)}` is the
weighted sum `∑ᵢ αⁱ(x) f(Φᵢ(x))` (no integrability needed: each `δ` integrates every function). -/
theorem integral_egfKernel {X : Type*} [MeasurableSpace X] [MeasurableSingletonClass X] {p : ℕ}
    (Φ : Fin p → X → X) (α : Fin p → X → ℝ) (hΦ : ∀ i, Measurable (Φ i))
    (hα : ∀ i, Measurable (α i)) (hα0 : ∀ i x, 0 ≤ α i x) (f : X → ℝ) (x : X) :
    ∫ y, f y ∂(egfKernel Φ α hΦ hα x) = ∑ i, α i x * f (Φ i x) := by
  show ∫ y, f y ∂(∑ i, ENNReal.ofReal (α i x) • Measure.dirac (Φ i x)) = _
  rw [integral_finsetSum_measure fun i _ =>
    (integrable_dirac enorm_lt_top).smul_measure ENNReal.ofReal_ne_top]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
  rw [integral_smul_measure, integral_dirac, ENNReal.toReal_ofReal (hα0 i x), smul_eq_mul]

/-- **The uniform EGF kernel of rotations** `π(x) = (1/p) ∑ᵢ δ_{Φᵢ x}` on `S^{n−1}`
(`main.tex:832`: "`∀ i, αⁱ = 1/p`", the kernel of `equ:forward_policy`). -/
noncomputable def sphereUniformKernel {n p : ℕ} (Φ : Fin p → SO n) :
    Kernel (RoundSphere n) (RoundSphere n) :=
  egfKernel (fun i => rotSphere (Φ i)) (fun _ _ => 1 / (p : ℝ))
    (fun i => measurable_rotSphere (Φ i)) fun _ => measurable_const

theorem isEGFPolicy_sphereUniformKernel {n p : ℕ} (hp : 0 < p) (Φ : Fin p → SO n) :
    IsEGFPolicy (sphereUniformKernel Φ) (fun i => rotSphere (Φ i)) (fun _ _ => 1 / (p : ℝ)) :=
  isEGFPolicy_egfKernel _ _ _ _ (fun _ _ => by positivity) fun _ => by
    rw [Finset.sum_const, Finset.card_univ, Fintype.card_fin, nsmul_eq_mul]
    field_simp

theorem integral_sphereUniformKernel {n p : ℕ} (Φ : Fin p → SO n) (f : RoundSphere n → ℝ)
    (x : RoundSphere n) :
    ∫ y, f y ∂(sphereUniformKernel Φ x) = ∑ i, 1 / (p : ℝ) * f (rotSphere (Φ i) x) :=
  integral_egfKernel _ _ _ _ (fun _ _ => by positivity) f x

/-- **Bourgain–Gamburd's one-sided spectral gap** for a Markov kernel `π` on `(X, μ)`
(arXiv:1108.6264v1, p. 1: `λ₁(z) < 2k`; `main.tex:273`: "the spectrum of the Koopman operator is
bounded away from 1 on `{φ | ∫ φ dλ = 0}`"): the quadratic form of the Markov operator
`Pf(x) = ∫ f dπ(x)` on the real `L²₀(μ)` is bounded by `c‖f‖²` for some `c < 1`. It is the
quadratic form of the paper's Koopman operator `φ ↦ d((φλ)π)/dλ` too, its `L²(μ)`-adjoint (not
formalized). -/
def HasBGSpectralGap {X : Type*} [MeasurableSpace X] (π : Kernel X X) (μ : Measure X) : Prop :=
  ∃ c : ℝ, c < 1 ∧ ∀ f : X → ℝ, MemLp f 2 μ → ∫ x, f x ∂μ = 0 →
    ∫ x, (∫ y, f y ∂(π x)) * f x ∂μ ≤ c * ∫ x, f x ^ 2 ∂μ

/-- **`theo:spectral_gap_sphere` as printed** (`main.tex:830–833`, "Reformulation of Theorem 1 of
`bourgain2012spectral`"), for `SO(n)` acting on `S^{n−1}`: rotations `Φ₁, …, Φₚ ∈ SO(n)` with
algebraic entries, generating a dense subgroup of `SO(n)`, the set stable under inverse, give the
uniform kernel a spectral gap (Bourgain–Gamburd's one-sided notion). Kept as a `Prop` beside its
refutation at `n = 2` (`not_spectralGapSphereReformulation_two`). -/
def SpectralGapSphereReformulation (n : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∀ (p : ℕ) (Φ : Fin p → SO n),
    (∀ i a b, IsAlgebraic ℤ ((Φ i : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ) a b)) →
    Dense ((Subgroup.closure (Set.range Φ) : Subgroup (SO n)) : Set (SO n)) →
    (∀ i, ∃ j, Φ j = (Φ i)⁻¹) →
    HasBGSpectralGap (sphereUniformKernel Φ) (sphereVolume n)

/-! ## A one-sided spectral gap makes the moves ergodic (the paper's route, `main.tex:836`) -/

/-- **A one-sided spectral gap of the uniform EGF kernel makes the moves ergodic**: a set `A`
a.e.-invariant under every move with `0 < μ(A) < μ(X)` would give the fixed vector
`1_A − μ(A)/μ(X)` of `L²₀(μ)`, of positive norm. -/
theorem ergodic_of_hasBGSpectralGap {X : Type*} [MeasurableSpace X] [MeasurableSingletonClass X]
    {μ : Measure X} [IsFiniteMeasure μ] {p : ℕ} (hp : 0 < p) (Φ : Fin p → X → X)
    (hΦ : ∀ i, Measurable (Φ i))
    (h : HasBGSpectralGap (egfKernel Φ (fun _ _ => 1 / (p : ℝ)) hΦ fun _ => measurable_const) μ) :
    ∀ A, MeasurableSet A → (∀ i, Φ i ⁻¹' A =ᵐ[μ] A) → μ A = 0 ∨ μ Aᶜ = 0 := by
  intro A hA hinv
  by_contra hcon
  push Not at hcon
  obtain ⟨h0, h1⟩ := hcon
  obtain ⟨c, hc, hgap⟩ := h
  set a : ℝ := μ.real A / μ.real univ with ha
  set f : X → ℝ := fun x => A.indicator 1 x - a with hf
  have hfm : Measurable f := (measurable_one.indicator hA).sub measurable_const
  have hbd : ∀ x, ‖f x‖ ≤ 1 + |a| := by
    intro x
    rw [hf, Real.norm_eq_abs]
    refine (abs_sub _ _).trans (add_le_add ?_ le_rfl)
    by_cases hx : x ∈ A <;> simp [hx]
  have hmem : MemLp f 2 μ := MemLp.of_bound hfm.aestronglyMeasurable _ (ae_of_all _ hbd)
  have hU : μ.real univ ≠ 0 := by
    rw [measureReal_def]
    exact (ENNReal.toReal_pos (fun h => h0 (measure_mono_null (subset_univ _) h))
      (measure_ne_top _ _)).ne'
  have hint1 : Integrable (A.indicator (1 : X → ℝ)) μ := (integrable_const (1 : ℝ)).indicator hA
  have hmean : ∫ x, f x ∂μ = 0 := by
    show ∫ x, (A.indicator 1 x - a) ∂μ = 0
    rw [integral_sub hint1 (integrable_const a), integral_indicator_one hA, integral_const,
      smul_eq_mul, ha]
    field_simp
    ring
  have hPf : ∀ᵐ x ∂μ, (∫ y, f y ∂(egfKernel Φ (fun _ _ => 1 / (p : ℝ)) hΦ
      fun _ => measurable_const) x) * f x = f x ^ 2 := by
    have hall : ∀ᵐ x ∂μ, ∀ i, (Φ i x ∈ A ↔ x ∈ A) := by
      rw [ae_all_iff]
      intro i
      filter_upwards [hinv i] with x hx
      exact Iff.of_eq hx
    filter_upwards [hall] with x hx
    rw [integral_egfKernel _ _ _ _ (fun _ _ => by positivity)]
    have hfi : ∀ i, f (Φ i x) = f x := fun i => by
      simp only [hf]
      by_cases h : x ∈ A
      · simp [h, (hx i).2 h]
      · simp [h, show Φ i x ∉ A from fun h' => h ((hx i).1 h')]
    simp_rw [hfi]
    rw [Finset.sum_const, Finset.card_univ, Fintype.card_fin, nsmul_eq_mul]
    have hp' : (p : ℝ) ≠ 0 := by exact_mod_cast hp.ne'
    field_simp
  have hle := hgap f hmem hmean
  rw [integral_congr_ae hPf] at hle
  have hnn : 0 ≤ ∫ x, f x ^ 2 ∂μ := integral_nonneg fun x => sq_nonneg _
  have hzero : ∫ x, f x ^ 2 ∂μ = 0 := by nlinarith
  have hae : ∀ᵐ x ∂μ, f x ^ 2 = 0 := by
    have := (integral_eq_zero_iff_of_nonneg (fun x => sq_nonneg (f x)) hmem.integrable_sq).1 hzero
    filter_upwards [this] with x hx
    exact hx
  obtain ⟨x, hxA, hx⟩ := Measure.exists_mem_of_measure_ne_zero_of_ae h0 (ae_restrict_of_ae hae)
  obtain ⟨y, hyA, hy⟩ := Measure.exists_mem_of_measure_ne_zero_of_ae h1 (ae_restrict_of_ae hae)
  have hyA' : y ∉ A := hyA
  simp only [hf, Set.indicator_of_mem hxA, Pi.one_apply, pow_eq_zero_iff two_ne_zero,
    sub_eq_zero] at hx
  simp only [hf, Set.indicator_of_notMem hyA', pow_eq_zero_iff two_ne_zero, zero_sub,
    neg_eq_zero] at hy
  rw [← hx] at hy
  exact one_ne_zero hy


/-! ## The circle `S¹ ⊂ ℝ²`: rotations as unit complex numbers -/

/-- A continuous function on a sphere is integrable (the sphere is compact, `σ` finite). -/
theorem integrable_sphere_of_continuous {n : ℕ} {G : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup G]
    {F : RoundSphere n → G} (hF : Continuous F) : Integrable F (sphereVolume n) := by
  obtain ⟨C, hC⟩ := isCompact_univ.exists_bound_of_continuousOn hF.continuousOn
  exact Integrable.of_bound hF.aestronglyMeasurable C (ae_of_all _ fun x => hC x (mem_univ x))

/-- The complex coordinate `ζ(x) = x₀ + i x₁` of a point of `S¹ ⊂ ℝ²`. -/
noncomputable def zeta (x : RoundSphere 2) : ℂ :=
  ((x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2)) 0 : ℂ) + ((x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2)) 1 : ℂ) * Complex.I

theorem norm_zeta (x : RoundSphere 2) : ‖zeta x‖ = 1 := by
  have hx : ‖(x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2))‖ = 1 := mem_sphere_zero_iff_norm.1 x.2
  rw [EuclideanSpace.norm_eq, Fin.sum_univ_two] at hx
  rw [zeta, Complex.norm_add_mul_I]
  simpa [Real.norm_eq_abs, sq_abs] using hx

@[fun_prop] theorem continuous_zeta : Continuous zeta := by
  have h0 : Continuous fun x : RoundSphere 2 => (x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2)) 0 :=
    (PiLp.continuous_apply 2 _ 0).comp continuous_subtype_val
  have h1 : Continuous fun x : RoundSphere 2 => (x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2)) 1 :=
    (PiLp.continuous_apply 2 _ 1).comp continuous_subtype_val
  unfold zeta
  fun_prop

/-- The entries of a rotation of the plane: `A = [[a, −b], [b, a]]`, `a² + b² = 1`
(`Matrix.mem_specialOrthogonalGroup_fin_two_iff`). -/
theorem so2_entries (A : SO 2) :
    (A : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ) 0 0 = (A : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ) 1 1 ∧
      (A : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ) 0 1 = -(A : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ) 1 0 ∧
      (A : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ) 0 0 ^ 2 + (A : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ) 0 1 ^ 2 = 1 :=
  Matrix.mem_specialOrthogonalGroup_fin_two_iff.1 A.2

/-- The unit complex number `a + ib` of a rotation `[[a, −b], [b, a]]` of the plane. -/
noncomputable def rotUnit (A : SO 2) : ℂ :=
  ((A : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ) 0 0 : ℂ) + ((A : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ) 1 0 : ℂ) * Complex.I

theorem norm_rotUnit (A : SO 2) : ‖rotUnit A‖ = 1 := by
  obtain ⟨-, h2, h3⟩ := so2_entries A
  rw [rotUnit, Complex.norm_add_mul_I, show (A : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ) 1 0 ^ 2 =
    (A : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ) 0 1 ^ 2 by rw [h2, neg_sq], h3, Real.sqrt_one]

/-- **A rotation of `S¹` is a multiplication**: `ζ(Ax) = w_A ζ(x)`. -/
theorem zeta_rotSphere (A : SO 2) (x : RoundSphere 2) :
    zeta (rotSphere A x) = rotUnit A * zeta x := by
  obtain ⟨h1, h2, -⟩ := so2_entries A
  apply Complex.ext <;>
    simp [zeta, rotUnit, rotSphere_apply_coord, Fin.sum_univ_two, h1, h2] <;> ring

/-- The rotation of angle `t` of the plane. -/
noncomputable def rotMat (t : ℝ) : SO 2 :=
  ⟨!![Real.cos t, -Real.sin t; Real.sin t, Real.cos t], by
    rw [Matrix.of_mem_specialOrthogonalGroup_fin_two_iff]
    exact ⟨rfl, rfl, by rw [neg_sq]; exact Real.cos_sq_add_sin_sq t⟩⟩

theorem coe_rotMat (t : ℝ) : (rotMat t : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ) =
    !![Real.cos t, -Real.sin t; Real.sin t, Real.cos t] := rfl

theorem rotUnit_rotMat (t : ℝ) : rotUnit (rotMat t) = Complex.exp (t * Complex.I) := by
  rw [Complex.exp_mul_I, ← Complex.ofReal_cos, ← Complex.ofReal_sin]
  simp [rotUnit, coe_rotMat]

/-- **`∫ ζᵐ dσ = 0` for `m ≥ 1`**: the rotation of angle `π/m` multiplies `ζᵐ` by `−1` and preserves
`σ`. -/
theorem integral_zeta_pow {m : ℕ} (hm : 0 < m) : ∫ x, zeta x ^ m ∂(sphereVolume 2) = 0 := by
  have h := integral_comp_rotSphere (rotMat (Real.pi / m)) (fun x => zeta x ^ m)
  simp only [zeta_rotSphere, rotUnit_rotMat, mul_pow, ← Complex.exp_nat_mul] at h
  have he : Complex.exp (↑m * (↑(Real.pi / m) * Complex.I)) = -1 := by
    have hm' : (m : ℂ) ≠ 0 := by exact_mod_cast hm.ne'
    rw [show (m : ℂ) * ((Real.pi / m : ℝ) * Complex.I) = Real.pi * Complex.I by
      push_cast; field_simp]
    exact Complex.exp_pi_mul_I
  rw [he, integral_const_mul] at h
  linear_combination (-1 / 2 : ℂ) * h

/-- For `‖z‖ = 1`: `Re(wz) Re(z) = (Re(wz²) + Re w)/2`. -/
theorem re_mul_re_eq {w z : ℂ} (hz : ‖z‖ = 1) :
    (w * z).re * z.re = ((w * z ^ 2).re + w.re) / 2 := by
  have h : z.re * z.re + z.im * z.im = 1 := by
    have := Complex.normSq_eq_norm_sq z
    rw [hz, one_pow, Complex.normSq_apply] at this
    linarith
  simp only [Complex.mul_re, Complex.mul_im, sq]
  linear_combination (w.re / 2) * h

/-- **The quadratic form on the characters**: `∫ Re(w ζᵏ) Re(ζᵏ) dσ = Re(w) σ(S¹)/2`, `k ≥ 1`. -/
theorem integral_re_mul_re_zeta (w : ℂ) {k : ℕ} (hk : 0 < k) :
    ∫ x, (w * zeta x ^ k).re * (zeta x ^ k).re ∂(sphereVolume 2) =
      w.re * (sphereVolume 2).real univ / 2 := by
  have hz : ∀ x, ‖zeta x ^ k‖ = 1 := fun x => by rw [norm_pow, norm_zeta, one_pow]
  simp_rw [re_mul_re_eq (hz _), ← pow_mul]
  have hc : Continuous fun x => w * zeta x ^ (k * 2) := continuous_const.mul (continuous_zeta.pow _)
  have hre := integral_re (𝕜 := ℂ) (integrable_sphere_of_continuous hc)
  simp only [RCLike.re_to_complex] at hre
  have hi1 : Integrable (fun x => (w * zeta x ^ (k * 2)).re) (sphereVolume 2) :=
    integrable_sphere_of_continuous (Complex.continuous_re.comp hc)
  rw [integral_div, integral_add hi1 (integrable_const _), hre, integral_const_mul,
    integral_zeta_pow (by positivity), mul_zero, Complex.zero_re, integral_const, smul_eq_mul]
  ring

/-- **Finitely many unit complex numbers have a common power near `1`** (compactness of the
torus `(S¹)ᵖ`). -/
theorem exists_pow_near_one {p : ℕ} (w : Fin p → ℂ) (hw : ∀ i, ‖w i‖ = 1) {ε : ℝ} (hε : 0 < ε) :
    ∃ k : ℕ, 0 < k ∧ ∀ i, ‖w i ^ k - 1‖ < ε := by
  set K : Set (Fin p → ℂ) := Set.pi univ fun _ => Metric.sphere (0 : ℂ) 1
  have hK : IsCompact K := isCompact_univ_pi fun _ => isCompact_sphere 0 1
  set u : ℕ → (Fin p → ℂ) := fun k i => w i ^ k
  have hu : ∀ k, u k ∈ K := fun k i _ => by simp [u, norm_pow, hw]
  obtain ⟨a, -, φ, hφ, hlim⟩ := hK.tendsto_subseq hu
  obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := Metric.cauchySeq_iff'.1 hlim.cauchySeq ε hε
  have h := hN (N + 1) (Nat.le_succ N)
  have hlt : φ N < φ (N + 1) := hφ (Nat.lt_succ_self N)
  refine ⟨φ (N + 1) - φ N, Nat.sub_pos_of_lt hlt, fun i => ?_⟩
  have hi := (dist_pi_lt_iff hε).1 h i
  simp only [Function.comp_apply, u, dist_eq_norm] at hi
  rwa [show φ (N + 1) = φ N + (φ (N + 1) - φ N) by omega, pow_add, ← mul_sub_one, norm_mul,
    norm_pow, hw, one_pow, one_mul] at hi

/-- **No finite set of rotations of `S¹` has a spectral gap** (C-28 (b), C-32), in
Bourgain–Gamburd's one-sided sense: for `p ≥ 1` rotations `Φᵢ` of the plane, with `wᵢ` their
unit complex numbers, the characters `fₖ = Re ζᵏ` (`k ≥ 1`) have mean zero and
`⟨Pfₖ, fₖ⟩ = (1/p ∑ᵢ Re wᵢᵏ) ‖fₖ‖²`, and some `k ≥ 1` brings every `wᵢᵏ` as close to `1` as
wished. -/
theorem not_hasBGSpectralGap_sphere_two {p : ℕ} (hp : 0 < p) (Φ : Fin p → SO 2) :
    ¬ HasBGSpectralGap (sphereUniformKernel Φ) (sphereVolume 2) := by
  rintro ⟨c, hc, hgap⟩
  set S := (sphereVolume 2).real univ with hS
  have hSpos : 0 < S := by
    rw [hS, measureReal_def]
    refine ENNReal.toReal_pos ?_ (measure_ne_top _ _)
    rw [sphereVolume, Measure.toSphere_apply_univ]
    refine mul_ne_zero (by simp) (Metric.measure_ball_pos volume _ one_pos).ne'
  set w : Fin p → ℂ := fun i => rotUnit (Φ i) with hw
  have key : ∀ k : ℕ, 0 < k → 1 / (p : ℝ) * ∑ i, (w i ^ k).re ≤ c := by
    intro k hk
    set f : RoundSphere 2 → ℝ := fun x => (zeta x ^ k).re with hf
    have hzk : Continuous fun x => zeta x ^ k := continuous_zeta.pow k
    have hfc : Continuous f := Complex.continuous_re.comp hzk
    have hmem : MemLp f 2 (sphereVolume 2) :=
      MemLp.of_bound hfc.aestronglyMeasurable 1 (ae_of_all _ fun x =>
        (Complex.abs_re_le_norm _).trans (by rw [norm_pow, norm_zeta, one_pow]))
    have hmean : ∫ x, f x ∂(sphereVolume 2) = 0 := by
      have hre := integral_re (𝕜 := ℂ) (integrable_sphere_of_continuous hzk)
      simp only [RCLike.re_to_complex] at hre
      rw [hf, hre, integral_zeta_pow hk, Complex.zero_re]
    have hle := hgap f hmem hmean
    have hP : ∀ x, (∫ y, f y ∂(sphereUniformKernel Φ x)) * f x =
        ∑ i, 1 / (p : ℝ) * ((w i ^ k * zeta x ^ k).re * (zeta x ^ k).re) := by
      intro x
      rw [integral_sphereUniformKernel, Finset.sum_mul]
      refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
      simp only [hf, hw, zeta_rotSphere, mul_pow]
      ring
    simp_rw [hP] at hle
    have hint : ∀ i ∈ Finset.univ, Integrable (fun x => 1 / (p : ℝ) *
        ((w i ^ k * zeta x ^ k).re * (zeta x ^ k).re)) (sphereVolume 2) := fun i _ =>
      integrable_sphere_of_continuous (by fun_prop)
    rw [integral_finsetSum _ hint] at hle
    simp_rw [integral_const_mul, integral_re_mul_re_zeta _ hk] at hle
    have hf2 : ∫ x, f x ^ 2 ∂(sphereVolume 2) = S / 2 := by
      have h1 := integral_re_mul_re_zeta 1 hk
      simp only [one_mul, Complex.one_re] at h1
      simp_rw [hf, sq]
      rw [h1, hS]
    rw [hf2] at hle
    have hsum : ∑ i, 1 / (p : ℝ) * ((w i ^ k).re * S / 2) =
        (1 / (p : ℝ) * ∑ i, (w i ^ k).re) * (S / 2) := by
      rw [Finset.mul_sum, Finset.sum_mul]
      exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => by ring
    rw [hsum] at hle
    exact le_of_mul_le_mul_right hle (by positivity)
  obtain ⟨k, hk, hclose⟩ := exists_pow_near_one w (fun i => norm_rotUnit (Φ i))
    (ε := (1 - c) / 2) (by linarith)
  have hre : ∀ i, (1 + c) / 2 < (w i ^ k).re := by
    intro i
    have h1 := hclose i
    have h2 : -‖w i ^ k - 1‖ ≤ (w i ^ k - 1).re := neg_le_of_abs_le (Complex.abs_re_le_norm _)
    rw [Complex.sub_re, Complex.one_re] at h2
    linarith
  have hsum : ∑ _i : Fin p, (1 + c) / 2 < ∑ i, (w i ^ k).re :=
    Finset.sum_lt_sum_of_nonempty (Finset.univ_nonempty_iff.2 ⟨⟨0, hp⟩⟩) fun i _ => hre i
  rw [Finset.sum_const, Finset.card_univ, Fintype.card_fin, nsmul_eq_mul] at hsum
  have hk' := key k hk
  have hp' : (0 : ℝ) < p := by exact_mod_cast hp
  rw [div_mul_eq_mul_div, one_mul, div_le_iff₀ hp'] at hk'
  nlinarith


/-! ## Rotations of the plane by an angle; density of an irrational rotation in `SO(2)` -/

theorem rotMat_add (s t : ℝ) : rotMat (s + t) = rotMat s * rotMat t := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  show (rotMat (s + t) : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ) =
    (rotMat s : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ) * (rotMat t : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ)
  rw [coe_rotMat, coe_rotMat, coe_rotMat, Matrix.mul_fin_two, Real.cos_add, Real.sin_add]
  ext i j
  fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;> simp <;> ring

theorem rotMat_zero : rotMat 0 = 1 := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  show (rotMat 0 : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ) = 1
  rw [coe_rotMat, Matrix.one_fin_two]
  simp

/-- `t ↦ rotMat t` as a homomorphism `ℝ → SO(2)`. -/
noncomputable def rotHom : Multiplicative ℝ →* SO 2 where
  toFun t := rotMat t.toAdd
  map_one' := rotMat_zero
  map_mul' s t := rotMat_add s.toAdd t.toAdd

theorem rotMat_zsmul (n : ℤ) (t : ℝ) : rotMat (n • t) = rotMat t ^ n :=
  map_zpow rotHom (Multiplicative.ofAdd t) n

theorem rotMat_neg (t : ℝ) : rotMat (-t) = (rotMat t)⁻¹ :=
  map_inv rotHom (Multiplicative.ofAdd t)

theorem rotMat_two_pi : rotMat (2 * Real.pi) = 1 := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  show (rotMat (2 * Real.pi) : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ) = 1
  rw [coe_rotMat, Matrix.one_fin_two]
  simp

/-- **Every rotation of the plane has an angle**. -/
theorem exists_rotMat (A : SO 2) : ∃ t, rotMat t = A := by
  obtain ⟨h1, h2, -⟩ := so2_entries A
  have hz : ‖rotUnit A‖ = 1 := norm_rotUnit A
  have hz0 : rotUnit A ≠ 0 := by
    intro h; rw [h, norm_zero] at hz; exact zero_ne_one hz
  have hc : Real.cos (Complex.arg (rotUnit A)) = (A : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ) 0 0 := by
    rw [Complex.cos_arg hz0, hz, div_one]; simp [rotUnit]
  have hs : Real.sin (Complex.arg (rotUnit A)) = (A : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ) 1 0 := by
    rw [Complex.sin_arg, hz, div_one]; simp [rotUnit]
  refine ⟨Complex.arg (rotUnit A), Subtype.ext ?_⟩
  show (rotMat _ : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ) = A
  rw [coe_rotMat, hc, hs]
  ext i j
  fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;> simp [h1, h2]

theorem continuous_rotMat : Continuous rotMat := by
  refine continuous_induced_rng.2 ?_
  show Continuous fun t : ℝ => (!![Real.cos t, -Real.sin t; Real.sin t, Real.cos t] :
    Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ)
  refine continuous_pi fun i => continuous_pi fun j => ?_
  fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;> simp <;> fun_prop

/-- **An irrational rotation generates a dense subgroup of `SO(2)`**: the subgroup of `ℝ`
generated by `t` and `2π` is dense (`dense_addSubgroupClosure_pair_iff`). -/
theorem dense_zpowers_rotMat {t : ℝ} (ht : Irrational (t / (2 * Real.pi))) :
    Dense ((Subgroup.zpowers (rotMat t) : Subgroup (SO 2)) : Set (SO 2)) := by
  have hD : Dense (AddSubgroup.closure {t, 2 * Real.pi} : Set ℝ) :=
    dense_addSubgroupClosure_pair_iff.2 ht
  intro A
  obtain ⟨s, rfl⟩ := exists_rotMat A
  rw [mem_closure_iff]
  intro U hU hsU
  obtain ⟨r, hrU, hr⟩ := hD.inter_open_nonempty (rotMat ⁻¹' U) (hU.preimage continuous_rotMat)
    ⟨s, hsU⟩
  obtain ⟨m, n, rfl⟩ := AddSubgroup.mem_closure_pair.1 hr
  refine ⟨rotMat (m • t + n • (2 * Real.pi)), hrU, ?_⟩
  rw [rotMat_add, rotMat_zsmul, rotMat_zsmul, rotMat_two_pi, one_zpow, mul_one]
  exact Subgroup.zpow_mem_zpowers _ _

/-! ## The printed reformulation is false for `SO(2)` (C-32) -/

/-- The angle `θ = arccos(3/5)`: `cos θ = 3/5`, `sin θ = 4/5`. -/
noncomputable def angle35 : ℝ := Real.arccos (3 / 5)

theorem cos_angle35 : Real.cos angle35 = 3 / 5 := Real.cos_arccos (by norm_num) (by norm_num)

theorem sin_angle35 : Real.sin angle35 = 4 / 5 := by
  rw [angle35, Real.sin_arccos, show (1 : ℝ) - (3 / 5) ^ 2 = (4 / 5) ^ 2 by norm_num]
  exact Real.sqrt_sq (by norm_num)

/-- **`θ/(2π)` is irrational** (Niven's theorem: a rational multiple of `π` with a rational cosine
has cosine in `{0, ±1/2, ±1}`, and `cos θ = 3/5`). -/
theorem irrational_angle35 : Irrational (angle35 / (2 * Real.pi)) := by
  rintro ⟨q, hq⟩
  have hθ : ∃ r : ℚ, angle35 = r * Real.pi := ⟨2 * q, by
    push_cast
    rw [hq]
    field_simp⟩
  have h := niven hθ ⟨3 / 5, by rw [cos_angle35]; norm_num⟩
  rw [cos_angle35] at h
  norm_num at h

/-- A rational number is algebraic over `ℤ`. -/
theorem isAlgebraic_ratCast (q : ℚ) : IsAlgebraic ℤ (q : ℝ) := by
  rw [Rat.cast_def, div_eq_mul_inv]
  exact (isAlgebraic_int q.num).mul (isAlgebraic_nat q.den).inv

theorem isAlgebraic_rotMat {t : ℝ} (hc : IsAlgebraic ℤ (Real.cos t))
    (hs : IsAlgebraic ℤ (Real.sin t)) (a b : Fin 2) :
    IsAlgebraic ℤ ((rotMat t : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ) a b) := by
  rw [coe_rotMat]
  fin_cases a <;> fin_cases b
  · exact hc
  · exact hs.neg
  · exact hs
  · exact hc

/-- **The witness of C-32**: the rotation of cosine `3/5` and its inverse. -/
noncomputable def so2Witness : Fin 2 → SO 2 := ![rotMat angle35, rotMat (-angle35)]

theorem so2Witness_algebraic (i : Fin 2) (a b : Fin 2) :
    IsAlgebraic ℤ ((so2Witness i : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ) a b) := by
  have hc : IsAlgebraic ℤ (Real.cos angle35) := by
    rw [cos_angle35, show (3 / 5 : ℝ) = ((3 / 5 : ℚ) : ℝ) by push_cast; ring]
    exact isAlgebraic_ratCast _
  have hs : IsAlgebraic ℤ (Real.sin angle35) := by
    rw [sin_angle35, show (4 / 5 : ℝ) = ((4 / 5 : ℚ) : ℝ) by push_cast; ring]
    exact isAlgebraic_ratCast _
  fin_cases i
  · exact isAlgebraic_rotMat hc hs a b
  · refine isAlgebraic_rotMat ?_ ?_ a b
    · rw [Real.cos_neg]; exact hc
    · rw [Real.sin_neg]; exact hs.neg

theorem so2Witness_dense :
    Dense ((Subgroup.closure (Set.range so2Witness) : Subgroup (SO 2)) : Set (SO 2)) :=
  (dense_zpowers_rotMat irrational_angle35).mono (SetLike.coe_subset_coe.2
    (Subgroup.zpowers_le.2 (Subgroup.subset_closure ⟨0, rfl⟩)))

theorem so2Witness_inv (i : Fin 2) : ∃ j, so2Witness j = (so2Witness i)⁻¹ := by
  fin_cases i
  · exact ⟨1, by simp [so2Witness, rotMat_neg]⟩
  · exact ⟨0, by simp [so2Witness, rotMat_neg]⟩

/-- **The printed reformulation (`main.tex:830–833`) is false for `SO(2)`** (C-32): the rotation of
cosine `3/5` and its inverse have rational entries, generate a dense subgroup of `SO(2)` (Niven)
and form a set stable under inverse, while no finite set of rotations of `S¹` has a spectral gap
(`not_hasBGSpectralGap_sphere_two`). -/
theorem not_spectralGapSphereReformulation_two : ¬ SpectralGapSphereReformulation 2 := fun h =>
  not_hasBGSpectralGap_sphere_two two_pos so2Witness
    (h 2 so2Witness so2Witness_algebraic so2Witness_dense so2Witness_inv)


/-! ## Isometry spherical models and their families (`main.tex:302–303`) -/

/-- **An isometry spherical model** with `p` moves on `S^{n−1}` (`main.tex:302–303`; the paper's
`𝕊^d` is `n = d + 1`): a non-empty parameter type `Θ`; for each parameter `θ`, the rotations
`Φθᵢ ∈ SO(n)` (parameters of the family, `main.tex:302`; constant in `θ` when "frozen",
`main.tex:307`), a softmax head `αθ` (positive measurable weights summing to `1`) and a scalar
head `fθ` (the outflow density, clipped at `0`, of finite mass). The continuity of the family
and the "tractable model" are not encoded: the class is larger, and the refuting models are
continuous. -/
structure IsometrySphericalModel (n p : ℕ) where
  /-- The parameter space of the model. -/
  Θ : Type
  nonempty : Nonempty Θ
  /-- The rotations `Φᵢ`. -/
  rot : Θ → Fin p → SO n
  /-- The softmax head. -/
  α : Θ → Fin p → RoundSphere n → ℝ
  /-- The scalar head. -/
  f : Θ → RoundSphere n → ℝ
  measurable_α : ∀ θ i, Measurable (α θ i)
  α_pos : ∀ θ i s, 0 < α θ i s
  α_sum : ∀ θ s, ∑ i, α θ i s = 1
  lintegral_f_ne_top : ∀ θ, ∫⁻ s, ENNReal.ofReal (f θ s) ∂(sphereVolume n) ≠ ∞

/-- The EGF of the parameter `θ`: moves `x ↦ Φθᵢ x`, policy `Σᵢ αθⁱ δ_{Φθᵢ}`, outflow `fθ σ`. -/
noncomputable def IsometrySphericalModel.flow {n p : ℕ} (M : IsometrySphericalModel n p)
    (θ : M.Θ) : GenerativeFlow (RoundSphere n) where
  policy := egfKernel (fun i => rotSphere (M.rot θ i)) (M.α θ)
    (fun i => measurable_rotSphere (M.rot θ i)) (M.measurable_α θ)
  outflow := (sphereVolume n).withDensity fun s => ENNReal.ofReal (M.f θ s)
  isMarkovKernel_policy := (isEGFPolicy_egfKernel _ _ _ _ (fun i s => (M.α_pos θ i s).le)
    (M.α_sum θ)).isMarkovKernel
  isFiniteMeasure_outflow := isFiniteMeasure_withDensity (M.lintegral_f_ne_top θ)

theorem IsometrySphericalModel.isEGFPolicy_flow {n p : ℕ} (M : IsometrySphericalModel n p)
    (θ : M.Θ) :
    IsEGFPolicy (M.flow θ).policy (fun i => rotSphere (M.rot θ i)) (M.α θ) :=
  isEGFPolicy_egfKernel _ _ (fun i => measurable_rotSphere (M.rot θ i)) (M.measurable_α θ)
    (fun i s => (M.α_pos θ i s).le) (M.α_sum θ)

/-- **The isometry spherical family of a model** (`main.tex:302–303`): the image `θ ↦ flow θ` of
its parameter space, non-empty. -/
def isometrySphericalFamily {n p : ℕ} (M : IsometrySphericalModel n p) :
    Set (GenerativeFlow (RoundSphere n)) :=
  Set.range M.flow

theorem isometrySphericalFamily_nonempty {n p : ℕ} (M : IsometrySphericalModel n p) :
    (isometrySphericalFamily M).Nonempty :=
  haveI := M.nonempty
  Set.range_nonempty _

/-- **`𝓕` is an isometry spherical family** (`main.tex:303`): it is the family of some model. -/
def IsIsometrySphericalFamily (n p : ℕ) (𝓕 : Set (GenerativeFlow (RoundSphere n))) : Prop :=
  ∃ M : IsometrySphericalModel n p, 𝓕 = isometrySphericalFamily M

/-- **C-31's model richness**: the family contains `(π, f σ)` for the uniform kernel `π` of the
rotations `Φ` and every `f` of a set dense in the non-negative cone of `L²(σ)`. -/
def IsRichSphericalModel {n p : ℕ} (Φ : Fin p → SO n)
    (𝓕 : Set (GenerativeFlow (RoundSphere n))) : Prop :=
  ∃ D : Set (RoundSphere n → ℝ), IsDenseNonnegConeL2 (sphereVolume n) D ∧
    ∀ f ∈ D, ∃ F ∈ 𝓕, F.policy = sphereUniformKernel Φ ∧
      F.outflow = (sphereVolume n).withDensity fun s => ENNReal.ofReal (f s)

/-- A rich family has `p ≥ 1` moves: the policy of a member is a Markov kernel. -/
theorem IsRichSphericalModel.pos {n p : ℕ} (hn : 0 < n) {Φ : Fin p → SO n}
    {𝓕 : Set (GenerativeFlow (RoundSphere n))} (hrich : IsRichSphericalModel Φ 𝓕) : 0 < p := by
  obtain ⟨D, hdense, hD⟩ := hrich
  obtain ⟨f, hfD, -, -⟩ := hdense 0 MemLp.zero (fun _ => le_rfl) 1 one_pos
  obtain ⟨F, -, hFπ, -⟩ := hD f hfD
  rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos p with h0 | h0
  · subst h0
    obtain ⟨i⟩ : Nonempty (Fin n) := ⟨⟨0, hn⟩⟩
    set x : RoundSphere n := ⟨EuclideanSpace.single i 1, by simp⟩
    have h1 := (F.isMarkovKernel_policy.isProbabilityMeasure x).measure_univ
    rw [hFπ] at h1
    simp [sphereUniformKernel, egfKernel] at h1
  · exact h0

/-- **The `L²` model** at frozen rotations `Φ`: `Θ = {f ∈ L²(σ) | f ≥ 0}`, uniform softmax head,
scalar head `f`. It is rich (`isRichSphericalModel_l2`). -/
noncomputable def l2SphericalModel {n p : ℕ} (hp : 0 < p) (Φ : Fin p → SO n) :
    IsometrySphericalModel n p where
  Θ := {f : RoundSphere n → ℝ // MemLp f 2 (sphereVolume n) ∧ ∀ s, 0 ≤ f s}
  nonempty := ⟨⟨0, MemLp.zero, fun _ => le_rfl⟩⟩
  rot _ := Φ
  α _ _ _ := 1 / (p : ℝ)
  f θ := θ.1
  measurable_α _ _ := measurable_const
  α_pos _ _ _ := by positivity
  α_sum _ _ := by
    rw [Finset.sum_const, Finset.card_univ, Fintype.card_fin, nsmul_eq_mul]
    field_simp
  lintegral_f_ne_top θ := Markov.lintegral_ofReal_ne_top (θ.2.1.integrable one_le_two)

theorem isRichSphericalModel_l2 {n p : ℕ} (hp : 0 < p) (Φ : Fin p → SO n) :
    IsRichSphericalModel Φ (isometrySphericalFamily (l2SphericalModel hp Φ)) :=
  ⟨{f | MemLp f 2 (sphereVolume n) ∧ ∀ s, 0 ≤ f s},
    fun g hg hgnn η hη => ⟨g, ⟨hg, hgnn⟩, hg.1, by simpa using hη⟩,
    fun f hf => ⟨(l2SphericalModel hp Φ).flow ⟨f, hf⟩, ⟨⟨f, hf⟩, rfl⟩, rfl, rfl⟩⟩

/-! ## Theorem 3.6 from ergodicity (C-28, C-29, C-31) -/

/-- **Theorem 3.6, the strongest form proved here** (C-28 sphere half, C-29, C-31): if every set
a.e.-invariant under all the rotations `Φᵢ` is null or conull, and the family contains the
uniform kernel of the `Φᵢ` with outflows dense in the non-negative cone of `L²(σ)`
(`IsRichSphericalModel`), the family is ε-universal. No spectral gap, no algebraic entries, no
inverse-stability; any family, in particular `isometrySphericalFamily M` for a rich model `M`. -/
theorem universality_sphere_of_ergodic {n p : ℕ} (hn : 0 < n) (Φ : Fin p → SO n)
    (herg : ∀ A, MeasurableSet A → (∀ i, rotSphere (Φ i) ⁻¹' A =ᵐ[sphereVolume n] A) →
      sphereVolume n A = 0 ∨ sphereVolume n Aᶜ = 0)
    (𝓕 : Set (GenerativeFlow (RoundSphere n))) (hrich : IsRichSphericalModel Φ 𝓕) :
    IsUniversalFamilyEps (sphereVolume n) 𝓕 := by
  have hp := hrich.pos hn
  obtain ⟨D, hdense, hD⟩ := hrich
  obtain ⟨hinv, hke⟩ := isKernelErgodic_egfKernel_uniform hp (fun i => rotSphere (Φ i))
    (fun i => measurable_rotSphere (Φ i)) (fun i => measurePreserving_rotSphere (Φ i)) herg
  exact universality_of_ergodic_family (sphereVolume n) 𝓕 (sphereUniformKernel Φ)
    (sphereVolume n) hinv Measure.AbsolutelyContinuous.rfl Measure.AbsolutelyContinuous.rfl hke D
    hD hdense

/-- **The group generated by the rotations**, as permutations of the sphere. -/
noncomputable def sphereRotGroup {n p : ℕ} (Φ : Fin p → SO n) :
    Subgroup (Equiv.Perm (RoundSphere n)) :=
  Subgroup.closure (Set.range fun i => rotPerm (Φ i))

/-- **The generated group acts ergodically iff the moves have no common non-trivial
a.e.-invariant set** (the moves and their inverses preserve `σ`). -/
theorem isGroupErgodic_sphereRotGroup_iff {n p : ℕ} (Φ : Fin p → SO n) :
    IsGroupErgodic (sphereVolume n) (sphereRotGroup Φ) ↔
      ∀ A, MeasurableSet A → (∀ i, rotSphere (Φ i) ⁻¹' A =ᵐ[sphereVolume n] A) →
        sphereVolume n A = 0 ∨ sphereVolume n Aᶜ = 0 := by
  constructor
  · intro herg A hA hinv
    refine herg A hA fun h hh => ae_invariant_of_mem_closure ?_ ?_ hh
    · rintro g ⟨i, rfl⟩
      exact ⟨measurePreserving_rotSphere (Φ i), measurePreserving_rotSphere (Φ i)⁻¹⟩
    · rintro g ⟨i, rfl⟩
      exact hinv i
  · intro herg A hA hinv
    exact herg A hA fun i => hinv _ (Subgroup.subset_closure ⟨i, rfl⟩)

/-- **Theorem 3.6 under ergodicity of the generated group** (C-28, C-29, C-31). -/
theorem universality_sphere_of_groupErgodic {n p : ℕ} (hn : 0 < n) (Φ : Fin p → SO n)
    (herg : IsGroupErgodic (sphereVolume n) (sphereRotGroup Φ))
    (𝓕 : Set (GenerativeFlow (RoundSphere n))) (hrich : IsRichSphericalModel Φ 𝓕) :
    IsUniversalFamilyEps (sphereVolume n) 𝓕 :=
  universality_sphere_of_ergodic hn Φ ((isGroupErgodic_sphereRotGroup_iff Φ).1 herg) 𝓕 hrich

/-- **The uniform kernel is ergodic iff the generated group is** (`σ` is invariant for both). -/
theorem isKernelErgodic_sphereUniformKernel_iff {n p : ℕ} (hp : 0 < p) (Φ : Fin p → SO n) :
    IsKernelErgodic (sphereUniformKernel Φ) (sphereVolume n) ↔
      IsGroupErgodic (sphereVolume n) (sphereRotGroup Φ) := by
  rw [isGroupErgodic_sphereRotGroup_iff]
  constructor
  · intro hk E hE hinv
    refine hk E hE ?_
    have hall : ∀ᵐ x ∂(sphereVolume n), ∀ i, (rotSphere (Φ i) x ∈ E ↔ x ∈ E) := by
      rw [ae_all_iff]
      intro i
      filter_upwards [hinv i] with x hx
      exact Iff.of_eq hx
    have hone : (p : ℝ≥0∞) * ENNReal.ofReal (1 / (p : ℝ)) = 1 := by
      rw [ENNReal.ofReal_div_of_pos (by exact_mod_cast hp), ENNReal.ofReal_one,
        ENNReal.ofReal_natCast, one_div]
      exact ENNReal.mul_inv_cancel (by exact_mod_cast hp.ne') (ENNReal.natCast_ne_top p)
    filter_upwards [hall] with x hx
    rw [(isEGFPolicy_sphereUniformKernel hp Φ).apply_set x hE]
    have hi : ∀ i, E.indicator (1 : RoundSphere n → ℝ≥0∞) (rotSphere (Φ i) x) =
        E.indicator 1 x := fun i => by
      by_cases h : x ∈ E
      · rw [Set.indicator_of_mem h, Set.indicator_of_mem ((hx i).2 h), Pi.one_apply, Pi.one_apply]
      · rw [Set.indicator_of_notMem h, Set.indicator_of_notMem fun h' => h ((hx i).1 h')]
    simp_rw [hi]
    rw [Finset.sum_const, Finset.card_univ, Fintype.card_fin, nsmul_eq_mul, ← mul_assoc, hone,
      one_mul]
  · intro herg
    exact (isKernelErgodic_egfKernel_uniform hp _ (fun i => measurable_rotSphere (Φ i))
      (fun i => measurePreserving_rotSphere (Φ i)) herg).2

/-- **Ergodicity of the generated group is necessary and sufficient** (C-28, C-29): the family of
the `L²` model at frozen rotations `Φ` is ε-universal iff the group the `Φᵢ` generate acts
ergodically on `(S^{n−1}, σ)`. -/
theorem universality_sphere_iff {n p : ℕ} (hn : 0 < n) (hp : 0 < p) (Φ : Fin p → SO n) :
    IsUniversalFamilyEps (sphereVolume n) (isometrySphericalFamily (l2SphericalModel hp Φ)) ↔
      IsGroupErgodic (sphereVolume n) (sphereRotGroup Φ) := by
  refine ⟨fun hU => ?_, fun herg => universality_sphere_of_groupErgodic hn Φ herg _
    (isRichSphericalModel_l2 hp Φ)⟩
  haveI := (isEGFPolicy_sphereUniformKernel hp Φ).isMarkovKernel
  refine (isKernelErgodic_sphereUniformKernel_iff hp Φ).mp (by_contra fun herg => ?_)
  refine not_isUniversalFamilyEps_of_not_ergodic (sphereVolume n) _ (sphereUniformKernel Φ) ?_
    herg hU
  rintro F ⟨θ, rfl⟩
  exact ⟨rfl, withDensity_absolutelyContinuous _ _⟩

/-- **Theorem 3.6 by the paper's route** (`main.tex:836`): from the printed reformulation, read
as a named hypothesis at the index of the rotations (`SO(n)` on `S^{n−1}`), the frozen rotations
of `main.tex:836` (algebraic entries, dense, stable under inverse) are ergodic and the rich
family is ε-universal. The hypothesis is false for `n = 2`
(`not_spectralGapSphereReformulation_two`). -/
theorem universality_sphere_of_reformulation {n p : ℕ} (hn : 0 < n)
    (hR : SpectralGapSphereReformulation n) (Φ : Fin p → SO n)
    (halg : ∀ i a b, IsAlgebraic ℤ ((Φ i : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ) a b))
    (hdense : Dense ((Subgroup.closure (Set.range Φ) : Subgroup (SO n)) : Set (SO n)))
    (hinv : ∀ i, ∃ j, Φ j = (Φ i)⁻¹)
    (𝓕 : Set (GenerativeFlow (RoundSphere n))) (hrich : IsRichSphericalModel Φ 𝓕) :
    IsUniversalFamilyEps (sphereVolume n) 𝓕 :=
  universality_sphere_of_ergodic hn Φ (ergodic_of_hasBGSpectralGap (hrich.pos hn) _ _
    (hR p Φ halg hdense hinv)) 𝓕 hrich


/-! ## The printed Theorem 3.6 needs the model (C-31, sphere half) -/

/-- **The sphere has positive volume** (`n ≥ 1`): `σ(S^{n−1}) = n · vol(B(0, 1))`. -/
theorem sphereVolume_univ_ne_zero {n : ℕ} (hn : 0 < n) : sphereVolume n univ ≠ 0 := by
  rw [sphereVolume, Measure.toSphere_apply_univ]
  refine mul_ne_zero ?_ (Metric.measure_ball_pos volume _ one_pos).ne'
  simp [finrank_euclideanSpace, hn.ne']

/-- **A flow whose outflow is fixed by its policy cannot reduce the defect**: on a finite
`(X, λ)` with a measurable `E`, `λ(E) ≠ 0 ≠ λ(Eᶜ)`, a family all of whose members satisfy
`F_out π = F_out` is not ε-universal (from the normalized `λ|_{Eᶜ}` to the normalized `λ|_E`, the
defect is at least the total variation, at least `1`). The torus file's
`not_isUniversalFamilyEps_of_inflow_eq`, for any finite measure. -/
theorem not_isUniversalFamilyEps_of_inflow_eq_of_set {X : Type*} [MeasurableSpace X]
    (lam : Measure X) [IsFiniteMeasure lam] {E : Set X} (hE : MeasurableSet E)
    (h0 : lam E ≠ 0) (h1 : lam Eᶜ ≠ 0) (𝓕 : Set (GenerativeFlow X))
    (h𝓕 : ∀ F ∈ 𝓕, inflow F.policy F.outflow = F.outflow) : ¬ IsUniversalFamilyEps lam 𝓕 := by
  intro hU
  set a : ℝ≥0∞ := (lam E)⁻¹ with ha
  set b : ℝ≥0∞ := (lam Eᶜ)⁻¹ with hb
  have hat : a ≠ ∞ := ENNReal.inv_ne_top.2 h0
  have hbt : b ≠ ∞ := ENNReal.inv_ne_top.2 h1
  set μ₁ : Measure X := lam.withDensity (E.indicator fun _ => a)
  set μ₀ : Measure X := lam.withDensity (Eᶜ.indicator fun _ => b)
  have hμ₁ : μ₁ = a • lam.restrict E := by
    show lam.withDensity _ = _
    rw [withDensity_indicator hE, withDensity_const]
  have hμ₀ : μ₀ = b • lam.restrict Eᶜ := by
    show lam.withDensity _ = _
    rw [withDensity_indicator hE.compl, withDensity_const]
  have hP₁ : IsProbabilityMeasure μ₁ := ⟨by
    rw [hμ₁, Measure.smul_apply, Measure.restrict_apply MeasurableSet.univ, Set.univ_inter,
      smul_eq_mul, ha, ENNReal.inv_mul_cancel h0 (measure_ne_top _ _)]⟩
  have hP₀ : IsProbabilityMeasure μ₀ := ⟨by
    rw [hμ₀, Measure.smul_apply, Measure.restrict_apply MeasurableSet.univ, Set.univ_inter,
      smul_eq_mul, hb, ENNReal.inv_mul_cancel h1 (measure_ne_top _ _)]⟩
  have hbdd : ∀ {S : Set X} {c : ℝ≥0∞}, c ≠ ∞ → MeasurableSet S →
      ∃ C : ℝ≥0, ∀ᵐ s ∂lam, (lam.withDensity (S.indicator fun _ => c)).rnDeriv lam s ≤ C :=
    fun {S} {c} hc hS =>
      ⟨c.toNNReal, (Measure.rnDeriv_withDensity lam (measurable_const.indicator hS)).mono
        fun s hs => by
          rw [hs, ENNReal.coe_toNNReal hc]
          by_cases h : s ∈ S <;> simp [Set.indicator_of_mem, Set.indicator_of_notMem, h]⟩
  obtain ⟨F, hF, hlt⟩ := hU μ₁ μ₀ hP₁ hP₀ (withDensity_absolutelyContinuous _ _)
    (withDensity_absolutelyContinuous _ _) (hbdd hat hE) (hbdd hbt hE.compl) 1 one_pos
  have hle := tvMass_le_errors_of_inflow_eq F.policy F.outflow μ₀ μ₁ (h𝓕 F hF)
  have h1' : 1 ≤ tvMass μ₀ μ₁ := by
    have h : μ₀ ≤ (μ₀ - μ₁) + μ₁ := Measure.sub_le_iff_le_add.mp le_rfl
    have hle1 := h Eᶜ
    rw [Measure.add_apply] at hle1
    have hT : μ₀ Eᶜ = 1 := by
      rw [hμ₀, Measure.smul_apply, Measure.restrict_apply hE.compl, Set.inter_self, smul_eq_mul,
        hb, ENNReal.inv_mul_cancel h1 (measure_ne_top _ _)]
    have hF : μ₁ Eᶜ = 0 := by
      rw [hμ₁, Measure.smul_apply, Measure.restrict_apply hE.compl, Set.compl_inter_self,
        measure_empty, smul_zero]
    calc (1 : ℝ≥0∞) = μ₀ Eᶜ := hT.symm
      _ ≤ (μ₀ - μ₁) Eᶜ + μ₁ Eᶜ := hle1
      _ = (μ₀ - μ₁) Eᶜ := by rw [hF, add_zero]
      _ ≤ (μ₀ - μ₁) Set.univ := measure_mono (Set.subset_univ _)
      _ ≤ tvMass μ₀ μ₁ := le_self_add
  exact absurd (h1'.trans hle) (not_le.2 hlt)

/-- On `S^{n−1}`, `n ≥ 1`, the open hemisphere `{x₀ > 0}` and its complement are not null. -/
theorem exists_sphere_halves {n : ℕ} (hn : 0 < n) :
    ∃ E : Set (RoundSphere n), MeasurableSet E ∧ sphereVolume n E ≠ 0 ∧
      sphereVolume n Eᶜ ≠ 0 := by
  set i : Fin n := ⟨0, hn⟩
  have hc : Continuous fun x : RoundSphere n => (x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) i :=
    (PiLp.continuous_apply 2 _ i).comp continuous_subtype_val
  set e : RoundSphere n := ⟨EuclideanSpace.single i 1, by simp⟩
  set e' : RoundSphere n := ⟨EuclideanSpace.single i (-1), by simp⟩
  have hE : IsOpen {x : RoundSphere n | 0 < (x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) i} :=
    isOpen_lt continuous_const hc
  have hE' : IsOpen {x : RoundSphere n | (x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) i < 0} :=
    isOpen_lt hc continuous_const
  refine ⟨_, hE.measurableSet, hE.measure_ne_zero _ ⟨e, by simp [e]⟩, fun h => ?_⟩
  refine hE'.measure_ne_zero (sphereVolume n) ⟨e', by simp [e']⟩ (measure_mono_null ?_ h)
  intro x hx
  simp only [Set.mem_setOf_eq] at hx
  simp only [Set.mem_compl_iff, Set.mem_setOf_eq, not_lt]
  exact hx.le

/-- **A model whose heads ignore the state is never ε-universal** (C-31, sphere half): for
`n ≥ 1` and any isometry spherical model whose softmax head `αθ` and scalar head `fθ` are
constant in the state (rotations arbitrary, varying with `θ`), every member leaves `σ` invariant
and has `F_out = c σ`, so `F_out π = F_out`. -/
theorem not_isUniversalFamilyEps_sphere_of_constantHeads {n p : ℕ} (hn : 0 < n)
    (M : IsometrySphericalModel n p) (hα : ∀ θ i s s', M.α θ i s = M.α θ i s')
    (hf : ∀ θ s s', M.f θ s = M.f θ s') :
    ¬ IsUniversalFamilyEps (sphereVolume n) (isometrySphericalFamily M) := by
  obtain ⟨E, hE, h0, h1⟩ := exists_sphere_halves hn
  refine not_isUniversalFamilyEps_of_inflow_eq_of_set _ hE h0 h1 _ ?_
  rintro F ⟨θ, rfl⟩
  set s₀ : RoundSphere n := ⟨EuclideanSpace.single ⟨0, hn⟩ 1, by simp⟩
  have hpol := M.isEGFPolicy_flow θ
  have hinv : (sphereVolume n).bind (M.flow θ).policy = sphereVolume n := by
    rw [hpol.bind_eq_sum_map (sphereVolume n)]
    have hc : ∀ i, ((sphereVolume n).withDensity fun s => ENNReal.ofReal (M.α θ i s)).map
        (rotSphere (M.rot θ i)) = ENNReal.ofReal (M.α θ i s₀) • sphereVolume n := by
      intro i
      rw [show (fun s => ENNReal.ofReal (M.α θ i s)) = fun _ => ENNReal.ofReal (M.α θ i s₀) from
        funext fun s => by rw [hα θ i s s₀], withDensity_const, Measure.map_smul,
        (measurePreserving_rotSphere _).map_eq]
    simp_rw [hc]
    rw [← Finset.sum_smul, ← ENNReal.ofReal_sum_of_nonneg fun i _ => (M.α_pos θ i s₀).le,
      M.α_sum θ s₀, ENNReal.ofReal_one, one_smul]
  have hout : (M.flow θ).outflow = ENNReal.ofReal (M.f θ s₀) • sphereVolume n := by
    show (sphereVolume n).withDensity _ = _
    rw [show (fun s => ENNReal.ofReal (M.f θ s)) = fun _ => ENNReal.ofReal (M.f θ s₀) from
      funext fun s => by rw [hf θ s s₀], withDensity_const]
  rw [inflow, hout, Measure.bind_smul, hinv]

/-- **The constant model at frozen rotations `Φ`**: `Θ = ℝ≥0` (the outflow level `c`), uniform
softmax head, constant scalar head `c`. -/
noncomputable def constSphericalModelAt {n p : ℕ} (hp : 0 < p) (Φ : Fin p → SO n) :
    IsometrySphericalModel n p where
  Θ := ℝ≥0
  nonempty := ⟨0⟩
  rot _ := Φ
  α _ _ _ := 1 / (p : ℝ)
  f c _ := c
  measurable_α _ _ := measurable_const
  α_pos _ _ _ := by positivity
  α_sum _ _ := by
    rw [Finset.sum_const, Finset.card_univ, Fintype.card_fin, nsmul_eq_mul]
    field_simp
  lintegral_f_ne_top _ := by
    rw [lintegral_const]
    exact ENNReal.mul_ne_top ENNReal.ofReal_ne_top (measure_ne_top _ _)

/-- **The technical assumption of `main.tex:836`** for frozen rotations `Φᵢ ∈ SO(n)`: the set is
stable under inverse, the group it generates is dense (in `SO(n)`, the group the `Φᵢ` live in:
the reading of `main.tex:836`'s "`SO(d, ℝ)`" for the rotations of `𝕊^d`, `n = d + 1`), and every
entry is algebraic. -/
def IsPrintedSphereCondition {n p : ℕ} (Φ : Fin p → SO n) : Prop :=
  (∀ i, ∃ j, Φ j = (Φ i)⁻¹) ∧
    Dense ((Subgroup.closure (Set.range Φ) : Subgroup (SO n)) : Set (SO n)) ∧
    ∀ i a b, IsAlgebraic ℤ ((Φ i : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ) a b)

/-- **Theorem 3.6 as printed** (`main.tex:302–305`), with the technical assumption the appendix
states (`main.tex:836`): on `𝕊^d` (`RoundSphere (d + 1)`), every isometry spherical model whose
rotations meet that assumption at every parameter has an ε-universal family (the ε-form, weaker
than the exact Definition 3.2, so its refutation is the stronger). Kept as a `Prop` beside its
refutation. -/
def UniversalitySpherePrinted (d : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∀ (p : ℕ) (M : IsometrySphericalModel (d + 1) p), (∀ θ, IsPrintedSphereCondition (M.rot θ)) →
    IsUniversalFamilyEps (sphereVolume (d + 1)) (isometrySphericalFamily M)

/-- **The printed Theorem 3.6 is false as soon as its technical assumption is satisfiable**
(C-31): for `p ≥ 1` frozen rotations meeting `main.tex:836`, the constant model at these
rotations (a non-empty family, every member with these very moves) refutes it. -/
theorem not_universalitySpherePrinted {d p : ℕ} (hp : 0 < p) (Φ : Fin p → SO (d + 1))
    (hΦ : IsPrintedSphereCondition Φ) : ¬ UniversalitySpherePrinted d := fun hP =>
  not_isUniversalFamilyEps_sphere_of_constantHeads (Nat.succ_pos d) (constSphericalModelAt hp Φ)
    (fun _ _ _ _ => rfl) (fun _ _ _ => rfl) (hP p _ fun _ => hΦ)

/-- **On `𝕊¹` the printed Theorem 3.6 is false** (C-31): the rotation of cosine `3/5` and its
inverse meet `main.tex:836` (`so2Witness`), and the constant model at them is not ε-universal. -/
theorem not_universalitySpherePrinted_one : ¬ UniversalitySpherePrinted 1 :=
  not_universalitySpherePrinted two_pos so2Witness
    ⟨so2Witness_inv, so2Witness_dense, so2Witness_algebraic⟩


/-! ## `𝕊¹`: one irrational rotation is ergodic, so Theorem 3.6 holds on the circle -/

/-- The point of `S¹ ⊂ ℝ²` with complex coordinate `z`, `‖z‖ = 1`. -/
noncomputable def circleToSphere (z : Circle) : RoundSphere 2 :=
  ⟨WithLp.toLp 2 ![(z : ℂ).re, (z : ℂ).im], by
    rw [mem_sphere_zero_iff_norm, EuclideanSpace.norm_eq, Fin.sum_univ_two]
    have h := Circle.norm_coe z
    rw [← Complex.re_add_im (z : ℂ), Complex.norm_add_mul_I] at h
    simpa [Real.norm_eq_abs, sq_abs] using h⟩

/-- **`S¹ ⊂ ℝ²` is the unit circle of `ℂ`**, through `ζ` (a continuous bijection of a compact space
onto a Hausdorff one). -/
noncomputable def sphereTwoCircle : RoundSphere 2 ≃ₜ Circle :=
  Continuous.homeoOfEquivCompactToT2 (f :=
    { toFun := fun x => ⟨zeta x, mem_sphere_zero_iff_norm.2 (norm_zeta x)⟩
      invFun := circleToSphere
      left_inv := fun x => by
        apply Subtype.ext
        apply PiLp.ext
        intro i
        fin_cases i <;> simp [circleToSphere, zeta]
      right_inv := fun z => by
        apply Circle.ext
        simp only [zeta, circleToSphere]
        simp [Complex.re_add_im] })
    (continuous_zeta.subtype_mk _)

theorem coe_sphereTwoCircle (x : RoundSphere 2) : (sphereTwoCircle x : ℂ) = zeta x := rfl

/-- **The angle coordinate of `𝕊¹`**: `AddCircle (2π) ≃ₜ S¹`, `s ↦ (cos s, sin s)`. -/
noncomputable def angleToSphere : AddCircle (2 * Real.pi) ≃ₜ RoundSphere 2 :=
  AddCircle.homeomorphCircle'.trans sphereTwoCircle.symm

/-- **Translating the angle by `t` is the rotation of angle `t`**. -/
theorem angleToSphere_add (a : AddCircle (2 * Real.pi)) (t : ℝ) :
    angleToSphere (a + t) = rotSphere (rotMat t) (angleToSphere a) := by
  obtain ⟨s, rfl⟩ := QuotientAddGroup.mk_surjective a
  apply sphereTwoCircle.injective
  apply Circle.ext
  have h1 : (sphereTwoCircle (rotSphere (rotMat t) (angleToSphere s)) : ℂ) =
      zeta (rotSphere (rotMat t) (angleToSphere s)) := rfl
  have h2 : zeta (angleToSphere s) = (sphereTwoCircle (angleToSphere s) : ℂ) := rfl
  have h3 : ∀ b, sphereTwoCircle (angleToSphere b) = AddCircle.homeomorphCircle' b := fun b =>
    sphereTwoCircle.apply_symm_apply _
  rw [h1, zeta_rotSphere, rotUnit_rotMat, h2, h3, h3]
  rw [show ((s : AddCircle (2 * Real.pi)) + (t : AddCircle (2 * Real.pi))) =
    ((s + t : ℝ) : AddCircle (2 * Real.pi)) from (AddCircle.coe_add _ s t).symm,
    AddCircle.homeomorphCircle'_apply_mk, AddCircle.homeomorphCircle'_apply_mk, Circle.coe_exp,
    Circle.coe_exp]
  push_cast
  rw [add_mul, Complex.exp_add, mul_comm]

/-- **An irrational rotation of `𝕊¹` is ergodic** for `σ`: transported to `AddCircle (2π)`, `σ` is
a translation-invariant finite measure, hence a non-zero multiple of the Haar measure
(`Measure.isAddInvariant_eq_smul_of_compactSpace`), and the translation by `t` is ergodic there
(`AddCircle.ergodic_add_right`, `t/(2π)` irrational). -/
theorem ergodic_rotSphere_two {t : ℝ} (ht : Irrational (t / (2 * Real.pi)))
    (A : Set (RoundSphere 2)) (hA : MeasurableSet A)
    (hinv : rotSphere (rotMat t) ⁻¹' A =ᵐ[sphereVolume 2] A) :
    sphereVolume 2 A = 0 ∨ sphereVolume 2 Aᶜ = 0 := by
  haveI : Fact (0 < 2 * Real.pi) := ⟨Real.two_pi_pos⟩
  set ψ := angleToSphere
  set ν : Measure (AddCircle (2 * Real.pi)) := (sphereVolume 2).map ψ.symm with hνdef
  have hψm : Measurable ψ := ψ.continuous.measurable
  have hψsm : Measurable ψ.symm := ψ.symm.continuous.measurable
  have hνψ : ν.map ψ = sphereVolume 2 := by
    rw [hνdef, Measure.map_map hψm hψsm]
    simp
  have hmp : MeasurePreserving ψ ν (sphereVolume 2) := ⟨hψm, hνψ⟩
  haveI : IsFiniteMeasure ν := Measure.isFiniteMeasure_map _ _
  haveI : ν.IsAddLeftInvariant := ⟨fun g => by
    obtain ⟨s, rfl⟩ := QuotientAddGroup.mk_surjective g
    have hcomm : (fun a => ((s : ℝ) : AddCircle (2 * Real.pi)) + a) ∘ ψ.symm =
        ψ.symm ∘ rotSphere (rotMat s) := by
      funext y
      apply ψ.injective
      simp only [Function.comp_apply, Homeomorph.apply_symm_apply]
      rw [add_comm, angleToSphere_add, Homeomorph.apply_symm_apply]
    rw [hνdef, Measure.map_map (measurable_const_add _) hψsm, hcomm,
      ← Measure.map_map hψsm (measurable_rotSphere _), (measurePreserving_rotSphere _).map_eq]⟩
  have hν := Measure.isAddInvariant_eq_smul_of_compactSpace ν
    (volume : Measure (AddCircle (2 * Real.pi)))
  set c := ν.addHaarScalarFactor volume
  have hc : c ≠ 0 := by
    intro h0
    apply sphereVolume_univ_ne_zero two_pos
    rw [← hνψ, Measure.map_apply hψm MeasurableSet.univ, hν, h0, zero_smul]
    rfl
  have hord : addOrderOf (t : AddCircle (2 * Real.pi)) = 0 := by
    rw [← AddCircle.denseRange_zsmul_iff, AddCircle.denseRange_zsmul_coe_iff]
    exact ht
  have herg : Ergodic (fun a : AddCircle (2 * Real.pi) => a + (t : AddCircle (2 * Real.pi)))
      volume := AddCircle.ergodic_add_right.2 hord
  have hB : MeasurableSet (ψ ⁻¹' A) := hψm hA
  have hpre : (fun a : AddCircle (2 * Real.pi) => a + (t : AddCircle (2 * Real.pi))) ⁻¹'
      (ψ ⁻¹' A) = ψ ⁻¹' (rotSphere (rotMat t) ⁻¹' A) := by
    ext a
    simp only [Set.mem_preimage]
    rw [angleToSphere_add]
  have hBinv : (fun a : AddCircle (2 * Real.pi) => a + (t : AddCircle (2 * Real.pi))) ⁻¹'
      (ψ ⁻¹' A) =ᵐ[ν] ψ ⁻¹' A := by
    rw [hpre]
    exact hmp.quasiMeasurePreserving.preimage_ae_eq hinv
  rw [hν, Measure.ae_smul_measure_eq hc] at hBinv
  rcases herg.quasiErgodic.ae_empty_or_univ₀ hB.nullMeasurableSet hBinv with h | h
  · left
    rw [← hmp.measure_preimage hA.nullMeasurableSet, hν, Measure.smul_apply, measure_congr h,
      measure_empty, smul_zero]
  · right
    rw [← hmp.measure_preimage hA.compl.nullMeasurableSet, Set.preimage_compl, hν,
      Measure.smul_apply, ae_eq_univ.1 h, smul_zero]

/-- **Theorem 3.6 on `𝕊¹`** (C-28 (b)): if one of the rotations is of angle `t` with `t/(2π)`
irrational and the model is rich, the isometry spherical family on `𝕊¹` is ε-universal. The
spectral-gap route of `main.tex:836` gives nothing here: no finite set of rotations of `𝕊¹` has a
spectral gap in Bourgain–Gamburd's one-sided sense (`not_hasBGSpectralGap_sphere_two`). -/
theorem universality_sphere_one {p : ℕ} (Φ : Fin p → SO 2) {i₀ : Fin p} {t : ℝ}
    (hi₀ : Φ i₀ = rotMat t) (ht : Irrational (t / (2 * Real.pi)))
    (𝓕 : Set (GenerativeFlow (RoundSphere 2))) (hrich : IsRichSphericalModel Φ 𝓕) :
    IsUniversalFamilyEps (sphereVolume 2) 𝓕 :=
  universality_sphere_of_ergodic two_pos Φ (fun A hA hinv =>
    ergodic_rotSphere_two ht A hA (hi₀ ▸ hinv i₀)) 𝓕 hrich

/-- **An instance**: on `𝕊¹`, the family of the `L²` model with the single frozen rotation of
cosine `3/5` is ε-universal, while its uniform kernel has no one-sided spectral gap
(`not_hasBGSpectralGap_sphere_two`). -/
theorem universality_sphere_one_witness :
    IsUniversalFamilyEps (sphereVolume 2)
      (isometrySphericalFamily (l2SphericalModel one_pos ![rotMat angle35])) :=
  universality_sphere_one _ (i₀ := 0) rfl irrational_angle35 _ (isRichSphericalModel_l2 _ _)


/-! ## Non-vacuity of the hypotheses of `BourgainGamburdTheorem1`: a dense algebraic pair in `SU(2)` -/

/-- **The closure of a one-parameter subgroup's lattice**: for a continuous homomorphism
`h : ℝ → G` with `h(2π) = 1` and `θ/(2π)` irrational, every `h(t)` lies in the closure of the
powers of `h(θ)`. -/
theorem mem_topologicalClosure_zpowers {G : Type*} [Group G] [TopologicalSpace G]
    [IsTopologicalGroup G] (h : Multiplicative ℝ →* G)
    (hc : Continuous fun t : ℝ => h (Multiplicative.ofAdd t))
    (h2π : h (Multiplicative.ofAdd (2 * Real.pi)) = 1) {θ : ℝ}
    (hθ : Irrational (θ / (2 * Real.pi))) (t : ℝ) :
    h (Multiplicative.ofAdd t) ∈
      (Subgroup.zpowers (h (Multiplicative.ofAdd θ))).topologicalClosure := by
  have hD : Dense (AddSubgroup.closure {θ, 2 * Real.pi} : Set ℝ) :=
    dense_addSubgroupClosure_pair_iff.2 hθ
  have hcl : IsClosed {t : ℝ | h (Multiplicative.ofAdd t) ∈
      (Subgroup.zpowers (h (Multiplicative.ofAdd θ))).topologicalClosure} :=
    (Subgroup.isClosed_topologicalClosure _).preimage hc
  have hsub : (AddSubgroup.closure {θ, 2 * Real.pi} : Set ℝ) ⊆
      {t : ℝ | h (Multiplicative.ofAdd t) ∈
        (Subgroup.zpowers (h (Multiplicative.ofAdd θ))).topologicalClosure} := by
    intro r hr
    obtain ⟨m, n, rfl⟩ := AddSubgroup.mem_closure_pair.1 (SetLike.mem_coe.1 hr)
    refine Subgroup.le_topologicalClosure _ ?_
    rw [ofAdd_add, map_mul, ofAdd_zsmul, ofAdd_zsmul, map_zpow, map_zpow, h2π, one_zpow, mul_one]
    exact Subgroup.zpow_mem_zpowers _ _
  exact hcl.closure_subset_iff.2 hsub (hD.closure_eq ▸ mem_univ t)

theorem exp_mul_I_mul_conj (t : ℝ) :
    Complex.exp (t * Complex.I) * conj (Complex.exp (t * Complex.I)) = 1 := by
  rw [Complex.mul_conj, Complex.normSq_eq_norm_sq, Complex.norm_exp_ofReal_mul_I]
  simp

theorem conj_exp_mul_I_mul (t : ℝ) :
    conj (Complex.exp (t * Complex.I)) * Complex.exp (t * Complex.I) = 1 := by
  rw [mul_comm, exp_mul_I_mul_conj]

/-- `diag(e^{it}, e^{−it}) ∈ SU(2)`. -/
noncomputable def suDiag (t : ℝ) : SU 2 :=
  ⟨!![Complex.exp (t * Complex.I), 0; 0, conj (Complex.exp (t * Complex.I))], by
    rw [Matrix.mem_specialUnitaryGroup_iff, Matrix.mem_unitaryGroup_iff]
    refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
    · ext i j
      fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;>
        simp [Matrix.mul_apply, Fin.sum_univ_two, Matrix.star_apply, exp_mul_I_mul_conj,
          conj_exp_mul_I_mul]
    · rw [Matrix.det_fin_two_of, exp_mul_I_mul_conj]
      ring⟩

/-- The real rotation of angle `t` as an element of `SU(2)`. -/
noncomputable def suRot (t : ℝ) : SU 2 :=
  ⟨!![(Real.cos t : ℂ), -(Real.sin t : ℂ); (Real.sin t : ℂ), (Real.cos t : ℂ)], by
    have h : (Real.cos t : ℂ) ^ 2 + (Real.sin t : ℂ) ^ 2 = 1 := by
      exact_mod_cast Real.cos_sq_add_sin_sq t
    rw [Matrix.mem_specialUnitaryGroup_iff, Matrix.mem_unitaryGroup_iff]
    refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
    · ext i j
      fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;>
        simp [Matrix.mul_apply, Fin.sum_univ_two, Matrix.star_apply, Complex.conj_ofReal,
          -Complex.ofReal_cos, -Complex.ofReal_sin] <;> first | linear_combination h | ring
    · rw [Matrix.det_fin_two_of]
      linear_combination h⟩

theorem coe_suDiag (t : ℝ) : (suDiag t : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) =
    !![Complex.exp (t * Complex.I), 0; 0, conj (Complex.exp (t * Complex.I))] := rfl

theorem coe_suRot (t : ℝ) : (suRot t : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) =
    !![(Real.cos t : ℂ), -(Real.sin t : ℂ); (Real.sin t : ℂ), (Real.cos t : ℂ)] := rfl


theorem conj_exp_ofReal_mul_I (x : ℝ) :
    conj (Complex.exp (x * Complex.I)) = Complex.exp ((-x : ℝ) * Complex.I) := by
  rw [← Complex.exp_conj]
  congr 1
  simp

theorem exp_ofReal_mul_I_mul (a b : ℝ) :
    Complex.exp (a * Complex.I) * Complex.exp (b * Complex.I) =
      Complex.exp ((a + b : ℝ) * Complex.I) := by
  rw [← Complex.exp_add]
  congr 1
  push_cast
  ring

theorem suDiag_add (s t : ℝ) : suDiag (s + t) = suDiag s * suDiag t := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  show (suDiag (s + t) : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) =
    (suDiag s : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) * (suDiag t : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ)
  rw [coe_suDiag, coe_suDiag, coe_suDiag, Matrix.mul_fin_two, exp_ofReal_mul_I_mul]
  ext i j
  fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;> simp [← map_mul, exp_ofReal_mul_I_mul]

theorem suDiag_zero : suDiag 0 = 1 := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  show (suDiag 0 : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) = 1
  rw [coe_suDiag, Matrix.one_fin_two]
  simp

theorem suDiag_two_pi : suDiag (2 * Real.pi) = 1 := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  show (suDiag (2 * Real.pi) : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) = 1
  have h : Complex.exp (((2 * Real.pi : ℝ) : ℂ) * Complex.I) = 1 := by
    push_cast; exact Complex.exp_two_pi_mul_I
  rw [coe_suDiag, Matrix.one_fin_two, h]
  simp

theorem suRot_add (s t : ℝ) : suRot (s + t) = suRot s * suRot t := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  show (suRot (s + t) : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) =
    (suRot s : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) * (suRot t : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ)
  rw [coe_suRot, coe_suRot, coe_suRot, Matrix.mul_fin_two, Real.cos_add, Real.sin_add]
  push_cast
  ext i j
  fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;> simp [-Complex.ofReal_cos, -Complex.ofReal_sin] <;> ring

theorem suRot_zero : suRot 0 = 1 := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  show (suRot 0 : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) = 1
  rw [coe_suRot, Matrix.one_fin_two]
  simp

theorem suRot_two_pi : suRot (2 * Real.pi) = 1 := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  show (suRot (2 * Real.pi) : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) = 1
  rw [coe_suRot, Matrix.one_fin_two]
  simp

noncomputable def suDiagHom : Multiplicative ℝ →* SU 2 where
  toFun t := suDiag t.toAdd
  map_one' := suDiag_zero
  map_mul' s t := suDiag_add s.toAdd t.toAdd

noncomputable def suRotHom : Multiplicative ℝ →* SU 2 where
  toFun t := suRot t.toAdd
  map_one' := suRot_zero
  map_mul' s t := suRot_add s.toAdd t.toAdd

theorem continuous_suDiag : Continuous suDiag := by
  refine continuous_induced_rng.2 ?_
  show Continuous fun t : ℝ => (!![Complex.exp (t * Complex.I), 0; 0,
    conj (Complex.exp (t * Complex.I))] : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ)
  refine continuous_pi fun i => continuous_pi fun j => ?_
  fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;> simp <;> fun_prop

theorem continuous_suRot : Continuous suRot := by
  refine continuous_induced_rng.2 ?_
  show Continuous fun t : ℝ => (!![(Real.cos t : ℂ), -(Real.sin t : ℂ); (Real.sin t : ℂ),
    (Real.cos t : ℂ)] : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ)
  refine continuous_pi fun i => continuous_pi fun j => ?_
  fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;> simp <;> fun_prop

/-- The entries of `U ∈ SU(2)`: `U = [[α, −γ̄], [γ, ᾱ]]` with `|α|² + |γ|² = 1`. -/
theorem su2_entries (U : SU 2) :
    (U : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) 1 1 = conj ((U : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) 0 0) ∧
      (U : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) 0 1 = -conj ((U : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) 1 0) ∧
      ‖(U : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) 0 0‖ ^ 2 + ‖(U : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) 1 0‖ ^ 2 = 1 := by
  set M := (U : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) with hM
  obtain ⟨hu, hdet⟩ := Matrix.mem_specialUnitaryGroup_iff.1 U.2
  have h1 : M * star M = 1 := Matrix.mem_unitaryGroup_iff.1 hu
  have h1' : star M * M = 1 := Matrix.mem_unitaryGroup_iff'.1 hu
  have hinv : star M = M.adjugate := by
    rw [← Matrix.inv_eq_right_inv h1, Matrix.inv_def, hdet, Ring.inverse_one, one_smul]
  rw [Matrix.adjugate_fin_two] at hinv
  have e00 := congrFun (congrFun hinv 0) 0
  have e01 := congrFun (congrFun hinv 0) 1
  simp [Matrix.star_apply] at e00 e01
  have hn := congrFun (congrFun h1' 0) 0
  simp [Matrix.mul_apply, Fin.sum_univ_two, Matrix.star_apply, Complex.conj_mul'] at hn
  refine ⟨e00.symm, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [e01, neg_neg]
  · exact_mod_cast hn


theorem exp_mul_mul_exp (x y r : ℂ) :
    Complex.exp x * r * Complex.exp y = r * Complex.exp (x + y) := by
  rw [Complex.exp_add]
  ring

/-- **Euler angles of `SU(2)`**: every `U ∈ SU(2)` is `diag(e^{iφ}, e^{−iφ}) R(s) diag(e^{iψ}, e^{−iψ})`. -/
theorem su2_euler (U : SU 2) : ∃ φ s ψ : ℝ, suDiag φ * suRot s * suDiag ψ = U := by
  obtain ⟨h11, h01, hn⟩ := su2_entries U
  set α := (U : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) 0 0 with hαdef
  set γ := (U : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) 1 0 with hγdef
  have hα1 : ‖α‖ ≤ 1 := by nlinarith [norm_nonneg γ, norm_nonneg α]
  set s := Real.arccos ‖α‖ with hs
  have hcos : Real.cos s = ‖α‖ := Real.cos_arccos (by linarith [norm_nonneg α]) hα1
  have hsin : Real.sin s = ‖γ‖ := by
    rw [hs, Real.sin_arccos, show 1 - ‖α‖ ^ 2 = ‖γ‖ ^ 2 by linarith]
    exact Real.sqrt_sq (norm_nonneg _)
  have hαe : ((‖α‖ : ℝ) : ℂ) * Complex.exp ((Complex.arg α : ℂ) * Complex.I) = α :=
    Complex.norm_mul_exp_arg_mul_I α
  have hγe : ((‖γ‖ : ℝ) : ℂ) * Complex.exp ((Complex.arg γ : ℂ) * Complex.I) = γ :=
    Complex.norm_mul_exp_arg_mul_I γ
  refine ⟨(Complex.arg α - Complex.arg γ) / 2, s, (Complex.arg α + Complex.arg γ) / 2,
    Subtype.ext ?_⟩
  show (suDiag _ : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) * (suRot s : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) *
    (suDiag _ : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) = U
  rw [coe_suDiag, coe_suRot, coe_suDiag, Matrix.mul_fin_two, Matrix.mul_fin_two, hcos, hsin]
  simp only [conj_exp_ofReal_mul_I]
  ext i j
  fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j
  · simp
    rw [← hαdef]
    conv_rhs => rw [← hαe]
    rw [exp_mul_mul_exp]
    congr 2
    ring
  · simp
    rw [h01]
    conv_rhs => rw [← hγe]
    rw [map_mul, Complex.conj_ofReal, conj_exp_ofReal_mul_I, exp_mul_mul_exp]
    congr 3
    push_cast
    ring
  · simp
    rw [← hγdef]
    conv_rhs => rw [← hγe]
    rw [exp_mul_mul_exp]
    congr 2
    ring
  · simp
    rw [h11]
    conv_rhs => rw [← hαe]
    rw [map_mul, Complex.conj_ofReal, conj_exp_ofReal_mul_I, exp_mul_mul_exp]
    congr 2
    push_cast
    ring


/-- **The witness of DEC-141's non-vacuity for Bourgain–Gamburd**: `diag(e^{iθ}, e^{−iθ})` and the
rotation of angle `θ`, `cos θ = 3/5`, in `SU(2)`. -/
noncomputable def su2Witness : Fin 2 → SU 2 := ![suDiag angle35, suRot angle35]

/-- **The witness generates a dense subgroup of `SU(2)`**: the closure of the generated group
contains both one-parameter subgroups (`θ/(2π)` irrational), hence every product given by the
Euler angles (`su2_euler`). -/
theorem su2Witness_dense :
    Dense ((Subgroup.closure (Set.range su2Witness) : Subgroup (SU 2)) : Set (SU 2)) := by
  set Γ := Subgroup.closure (Set.range su2Witness)
  have hD : ∀ t, suDiag t ∈ Γ.topologicalClosure := fun t =>
    Subgroup.topologicalClosure_mono (Subgroup.zpowers_le.2
      (Subgroup.subset_closure (Set.mem_range_self (0 : Fin 2))))
      (mem_topologicalClosure_zpowers suDiagHom continuous_suDiag suDiag_two_pi
        irrational_angle35 t)
  have hR : ∀ t, suRot t ∈ Γ.topologicalClosure := fun t =>
    Subgroup.topologicalClosure_mono (Subgroup.zpowers_le.2
      (Subgroup.subset_closure (Set.mem_range_self (1 : Fin 2))))
      (mem_topologicalClosure_zpowers suRotHom continuous_suRot suRot_two_pi
        irrational_angle35 t)
  intro U
  obtain ⟨φ, s, ψ, rfl⟩ := su2_euler U
  rw [← Subgroup.topologicalClosure_coe]
  exact Γ.topologicalClosure.mul_mem (Γ.topologicalClosure.mul_mem (hD φ) (hR s)) (hD ψ)

theorem isAlgebraic_complex_I : IsAlgebraic ℚ Complex.I :=
  IsAlgebraic.of_pow two_pos (by rw [Complex.I_sq]; exact isAlgebraic_one.neg)

theorem exp_angle35 : Complex.exp (angle35 * Complex.I) = 3 / 5 + 4 / 5 * Complex.I := by
  rw [Complex.exp_mul_I, ← Complex.ofReal_cos, ← Complex.ofReal_sin, cos_angle35, sin_angle35]
  push_cast
  ring

/-- **The witness has algebraic entries** (in `ℚ(i)`). -/
theorem su2Witness_algebraic (j a b : Fin 2) :
    IsAlgebraic ℚ ((su2Witness j : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) a b) := by
  have h35 : IsAlgebraic ℚ (3 / 5 : ℂ) := by
    have := isAlgebraic_rat ℚ (A := ℂ) (3 / 5)
    push_cast at this
    exact this
  have h45 : IsAlgebraic ℚ (4 / 5 : ℂ) := by
    have := isAlgebraic_rat ℚ (A := ℂ) (4 / 5)
    push_cast at this
    exact this
  have hexp : IsAlgebraic ℚ (Complex.exp (angle35 * Complex.I)) := by
    rw [exp_angle35]
    exact h35.add (h45.mul isAlgebraic_complex_I)
  have hconj : IsAlgebraic ℚ (conj (Complex.exp (angle35 * Complex.I))) := by
    rw [exp_angle35, map_add, map_mul, Complex.conj_I]
    have h3 : conj (3 / 5 : ℂ) = 3 / 5 := by
      rw [show (3 / 5 : ℂ) = ((3 / 5 : ℝ) : ℂ) by push_cast; ring, Complex.conj_ofReal]
    have h4 : conj (4 / 5 : ℂ) = 4 / 5 := by
      rw [show (4 / 5 : ℂ) = ((4 / 5 : ℝ) : ℂ) by push_cast; ring, Complex.conj_ofReal]
    rw [h3, h4]
    exact h35.add (h45.mul isAlgebraic_complex_I.neg)
  have hc : IsAlgebraic ℚ ((Real.cos angle35 : ℝ) : ℂ) := by
    rw [cos_angle35]; push_cast; exact h35
  have hs : IsAlgebraic ℚ ((Real.sin angle35 : ℝ) : ℂ) := by
    rw [sin_angle35]; push_cast; exact h45
  fin_cases j <;> fin_cases a <;> fin_cases b <;>
    simp only [su2Witness, coe_suDiag, coe_suRot, Fin.zero_eta, Fin.mk_one, Fin.isValue,
      Matrix.cons_val_zero, Matrix.cons_val_one, Matrix.of_apply,
      Matrix.cons_val', Matrix.empty_val', Matrix.cons_val_fin_one]
  all_goals first
    | exact hexp | exact hconj | exact isAlgebraic_zero | exact hc | exact hs | exact hs.neg

/-- **Non-vacuity of `BourgainGamburdTheorem1`** (DEC-141): its hypotheses hold for `d = 2`, `k = 2`
and the generators `su2Witness`, so the named `Prop` gives them a spectral gap. -/
theorem bourgainGamburd_hypotheses_witness :
    (∀ j a b, IsAlgebraic ℚ ((su2Witness j : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) a b)) ∧
      Dense ((Subgroup.closure (Set.range su2Witness) : Subgroup (SU 2)) : Set (SU 2)) :=
  ⟨su2Witness_algebraic, su2Witness_dense⟩

/-- Under `BourgainGamburdTheorem1`, the witness pair has a spectral gap: an instance of the
named `Prop` whose hypotheses are met. -/
theorem bourgainGamburd_witness_gap (hBG : BourgainGamburdTheorem1) :
    ∃ c : ℝ, c < 2 * (2 : ℕ) ∧ ∀ f : SU 2 → ℂ, MemLp f 2 (suHaar 2) → ∫ x, f x ∂(suHaar 2) = 0 →
      (∫ x, heckeOp su2Witness f x * conj (f x) ∂(suHaar 2)).re ≤
        c * ∫ x, ‖f x‖ ^ 2 ∂(suHaar 2) :=
  hBG 2 le_rfl 2 su2Witness su2Witness_algebraic su2Witness_dense


/-! ## On `𝕊¹` the printed density clause suffices (with C-31's richness) -/

theorem rotMat_nsmul (n : ℕ) (t : ℝ) : rotMat (n • t) = rotMat t ^ n :=
  map_pow rotHom (Multiplicative.ofAdd t) n

theorem so2_mul_comm (A B : SO 2) : A * B = B * A := by
  obtain ⟨s, rfl⟩ := exists_rotMat A
  obtain ⟨t, rfl⟩ := exists_rotMat B
  rw [← rotMat_add, ← rotMat_add, add_comm]

/-- **A dense subgroup of `SO(2)` generated by finitely many rotations has an irrational generator**:
if every generator had finite order, the generated group would lie in the closed subgroup
`{A | A^M = 1}` (`SO(2)` is abelian), which misses the rotation of angle `π/M`. -/
theorem exists_irrational_of_dense {p : ℕ} (Φ : Fin p → SO 2)
    (hdense : Dense ((Subgroup.closure (Set.range Φ) : Subgroup (SO 2)) : Set (SO 2))) :
    ∃ i t, Φ i = rotMat t ∧ Irrational (t / (2 * Real.pi)) := by
  by_contra hcon
  push Not at hcon
  have hfin : ∀ i, ∃ N : ℕ, 0 < N ∧ Φ i ^ N = 1 := by
    intro i
    obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := exists_rotMat (Φ i)
    have hq := hcon i t ht.symm
    unfold Irrational at hq
    push Not at hq
    obtain ⟨q, hq⟩ := hq
    refine ⟨q.den, q.den_pos, ?_⟩
    have hden : (q.den : ℝ) * t = (q.num : ℝ) * (2 * Real.pi) := by
      have h2π : (2 * Real.pi) ≠ 0 := by positivity
      have hq' : t = (q : ℝ) * (2 * Real.pi) := by rw [hq]; field_simp
      rw [hq', Rat.cast_def]
      have : (q.den : ℝ) ≠ 0 := by exact_mod_cast q.den_pos.ne'
      field_simp
    rw [← ht, ← rotMat_nsmul, nsmul_eq_mul, hden, ← zsmul_eq_mul, rotMat_zsmul, rotMat_two_pi,
      one_zpow]
  choose N hNpos hN using hfin
  set M := ∏ i, N i with hM
  have hMpos : 0 < M := Finset.prod_pos fun i _ => hNpos i
  let K : Subgroup (SO 2) :=
    { carrier := {A | A ^ M = 1}
      mul_mem' := fun {a b} ha hb => by
        simp only [Set.mem_setOf_eq] at ha hb ⊢
        rw [(Commute.mul_pow (so2_mul_comm a b) M), ha, hb, one_mul]
      one_mem' := by simp
      inv_mem' := fun {a} ha => by
        simp only [Set.mem_setOf_eq] at ha ⊢
        rw [inv_pow, ha, inv_one] }
  have hle : Subgroup.closure (Set.range Φ) ≤ K := by
    rw [Subgroup.closure_le]
    rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := Finset.dvd_prod_of_mem N (Finset.mem_univ i)
    show Φ i ^ M = 1
    rw [hM, hk, pow_mul, hN i, one_pow]
  have hcl : IsClosed (K : Set (SO 2)) := isClosed_eq (continuous_pow M) continuous_const
  have hall : ∀ A : SO 2, A ^ M = 1 := fun A =>
    hcl.closure_subset_iff.2 (SetLike.coe_subset_coe.2 hle) (hdense A)
  have h := hall (rotMat (Real.pi / M))
  rw [← rotMat_nsmul, nsmul_eq_mul,
    show (M : ℝ) * (Real.pi / M) = Real.pi by field_simp] at h
  have h00 := congrArg (fun A : SO 2 => (A : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ) 0 0) h
  simp [coe_rotMat] at h00
  norm_num at h00

/-- **Theorem 3.6 on `𝕊¹` under the printed density clause** (C-28, C-31): rotations generating a
dense subgroup of `SO(2)` and a rich model give an ε-universal family. No algebraic entries and no
inverse-stability are needed; with them it is the printed Theorem 3.6 on `𝕊¹` completed by C-31's
richness. -/
theorem universality_sphere_one_of_dense {p : ℕ} (Φ : Fin p → SO 2)
    (hdense : Dense ((Subgroup.closure (Set.range Φ) : Subgroup (SO 2)) : Set (SO 2)))
    (𝓕 : Set (GenerativeFlow (RoundSphere 2))) (hrich : IsRichSphericalModel Φ 𝓕) :
    IsUniversalFamilyEps (sphereVolume 2) 𝓕 := by
  obtain ⟨i, t, hi, ht⟩ := exists_irrational_of_dense Φ hdense
  exact universality_sphere_one Φ hi ht 𝓕 hrich


/-! ## The refutation is reading-free: eigenvalues of the witness accumulate at `1` -/

/-- **The witness kernel has eigenvalues `cos kθ → 1` on `L²₀(σ)`**: for every `ε > 0` there are
`k ≥ 1` and a real eigenvalue `μ ∈ (1 − ε, 1]` with `P fₖ = μ fₖ` pointwise, `fₖ = Re ζᵏ` bounded,
of mean zero and positive norm. So 1 is a limit of eigenvalues of `P` on `L²₀(σ)`, and the
refutation `not_spectralGapSphereReformulation_two` holds whether "spectral gap" is read on the
quadratic form, on the spectrum, or as the absence of almost invariant vectors. -/
theorem so2Witness_eigen {ε : ℝ} (hε : 0 < ε) :
    ∃ (k : ℕ) (μ : ℝ), 0 < k ∧ 1 - ε < μ ∧ μ ≤ 1 ∧
      MemLp (fun x => (zeta x ^ k).re) 2 (sphereVolume 2) ∧
      ∫ x, (zeta x ^ k).re ∂(sphereVolume 2) = 0 ∧
      0 < ∫ x, (zeta x ^ k).re ^ 2 ∂(sphereVolume 2) ∧
      ∀ x, ∫ y, (zeta y ^ k).re ∂(sphereUniformKernel so2Witness x) = μ * (zeta x ^ k).re := by
  set w : ℂ := rotUnit (rotMat angle35) with hwdef
  have hw : ‖w‖ = 1 := norm_rotUnit _
  obtain ⟨k, hk, hclose⟩ := exists_pow_near_one (fun _ : Fin 1 => w) (fun _ => hw) hε
  have hk1 := hclose 0
  have hwconj : rotUnit (rotMat (-angle35)) = conj w := by
    rw [rotUnit_rotMat, hwdef, rotUnit_rotMat, ← Complex.exp_conj]
    congr 1
    simp
  have hzk : Continuous fun x => zeta x ^ k := continuous_zeta.pow k
  refine ⟨k, (w ^ k).re, hk, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, fun x => ?_⟩
  · have h2 : -‖w ^ k - 1‖ ≤ (w ^ k - 1).re := neg_le_of_abs_le (Complex.abs_re_le_norm _)
    rw [Complex.sub_re, Complex.one_re] at h2
    linarith
  · calc (w ^ k).re ≤ ‖w ^ k‖ := Complex.re_le_norm _
      _ = 1 := by rw [norm_pow, hw, one_pow]
  · exact MemLp.of_bound (Complex.continuous_re.comp hzk).aestronglyMeasurable 1
      (ae_of_all _ fun x => (Complex.abs_re_le_norm _).trans (by rw [norm_pow, norm_zeta, one_pow]))
  · have hre := integral_re (𝕜 := ℂ) (integrable_sphere_of_continuous hzk)
    simp only [RCLike.re_to_complex] at hre
    rw [hre, integral_zeta_pow hk, Complex.zero_re]
  · have h1 := integral_re_mul_re_zeta 1 hk
    simp only [one_mul, Complex.one_re] at h1
    simp_rw [sq]
    rw [h1]
    have hS : 0 < (sphereVolume 2).real univ := by
      rw [measureReal_def]
      exact ENNReal.toReal_pos (sphereVolume_univ_ne_zero two_pos) (measure_ne_top _ _)
    linarith
  · rw [integral_sphereUniformKernel, Fin.sum_univ_two]
    simp only [so2Witness, Matrix.cons_val_zero, Matrix.cons_val_one, zeta_rotSphere, mul_pow]
    rw [hwconj, ← map_pow]
    simp only [Complex.mul_re, Complex.conj_re, Complex.conj_im]
    push_cast
    ring

/-! ## `main.tex:307` as printed omits density -/

/-- **"Algebraic coefficients and frozen" (`main.tex:307`) is not sufficient**: the identity
rotation has integer entries and is frozen, yet the family of the `L²` model with it (the richest
model) is not ε-universal on `S^{n−1}`, `n ≥ 1`, since the identity is not ergodic. -/
theorem not_universality_sphere_identity {n : ℕ} (hn : 0 < n) :
    (∀ a b, IsAlgebraic ℤ (((1 : SO n) : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ) a b)) ∧
      ¬ IsUniversalFamilyEps (sphereVolume n)
        (isometrySphericalFamily (l2SphericalModel one_pos ![(1 : SO n)])) := by
  refine ⟨fun a b => ?_, fun hU => ?_⟩
  · show IsAlgebraic ℤ ((1 : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ) a b)
    rw [Matrix.one_apply]
    split_ifs
    · exact isAlgebraic_one
    · exact isAlgebraic_zero
  · have herg := (universality_sphere_iff hn one_pos _).1 hU
    obtain ⟨E, hE, h0, h1⟩ := exists_sphere_halves hn
    have hid : rotSphere (1 : SO n) = id := funext rotSphere_one
    rcases (isGroupErgodic_sphereRotGroup_iff _).1 herg E hE (fun i =>
      Filter.EventuallyEq.of_eq (by
        rw [show (![(1 : SO n)] i) = 1 by fin_cases i; rfl, hid, Set.preimage_id]))
      with h | h
    · exact h0 h
    · exact h1 h

end EGF
